1
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:52,636
{\i1}- Yeah. Is everything in place?
- You weren't supposed to relieve me.{\i}

2
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:55,394
{\i1}I know, but I felt like taking a shift.{\i}

3
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:58,195
{\i1}You like him, don 't you?
You like watching him.{\i}

4
00:00:58,440 --> 00:01:01,318
{\i1}- Don 't be ridiculous.
- We're gonna kill him. You understand that?{\i}

5
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:03,949
{\i1}Morpheus believes he is the One.{\i}

6
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:06,998
{\i1}- Do you?
- It doesn't matter what I believe.{\i}

7
00:01:07,240 --> 00:01:08,798
{\i1}You don't, do you?{\i}

8
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:11,031
{\i1}- Did you hear that?
- Hear what?{\i}

9
00:01:11,280 --> 00:01:12,793
{\i1}Are you sure this line is clean?{\i}

10
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:14,951
{\i1}Yeah, of course I'm sure.{\i}

11
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:16,679
{\i1}I better go.{\i}

12
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:54,798
- Freeze! Police!
- Hands on your head!

13
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:56,355
Do it!
Do it now!

14
00:02:16,880 --> 00:02:18,154
Lieutenant.

15
00:02:18,154 --> 00:02:19,389
Oh, shit.

16
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:23,272
Lieutenant, you were given
specific orders.

17
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:25,158
Hey.
I'm just doing my job.

18
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:29,992
You give me that "juris-my-dick-tion"
crap, you can cram it up your ass.

19
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:32,829
The orders were for your protection.

20
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:36,396
I think we are going to handle
one little girl.

21
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:42,992
I sent two units!

22
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:44,753
They're bringing her down now!

23
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,992
No, Lieutenant, your men
are already dead.

24
00:03:15,880 --> 00:03:16,915
Shit.

25
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:21,715
Morpheus, the line was traced.
I don't know how.

26
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:23,473
{\i1}I know. They cut the hard line.{\i}

27
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:25,790
{\i1}There's no time.
You are going have to get to another exit.{\i}

28
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:28,349
{\i1}- Are there any agents?
- Yes.{\i}

29
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:29,675
Goddamn it.

30
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:31,399
{\i1}You have to focus, Trinity.{\i}

31
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:33,915
{\i1}There's a phone at Wells and Lake.{\i}

32
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:35,872
{\i1}You can make it.{\i}

33
00:03:36,120 --> 00:03:37,712
{\i1}- All right.
- Go.{\i}

34
00:04:37,320 --> 00:04:38,309
That's impossible.

35
00:05:11,880 --> 00:05:13,836
Get up, Trinity.
Just get up.

36
00:05:14,440 --> 00:05:15,589
Get up.

37
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:01,033
She got out.

38
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:02,548
It doesn't matter.

39
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:04,791
The informant is real.

40
00:06:06,080 --> 00:06:07,672
We have the name of their next target.

41
00:06:07,920 --> 00:06:09,512
The name is Neo.

42
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:14,113
We'll need a search running.

43
00:06:14,400 --> 00:06:16,231
It has already begun.

44
00:07:08,760 --> 00:07:09,909
What?

45
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:16,873
What the hell?

46
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:26,077
"Follow the white rabbit."

47
00:07:37,440 --> 00:07:38,555
Who is it?

48
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:40,028
It's Choi.

49
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:54,115
You're two hours late.

50
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:56,352
I know. It's her fault.

51
00:07:56,640 --> 00:07:58,596
You got the money?

52
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:00,715
Two grand.

53
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:02,629
Hold on.

54
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:20,919
Hallelujah.

55
00:08:21,160 --> 00:08:23,913
You're my savior, man.
My own personal Jesus Christ.

56
00:08:24,160 --> 00:08:25,957
You get caught using that...

57
00:08:26,200 --> 00:08:28,236
Yeah. I know. This never happened.
You don't exist.

58
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:31,311
- Right.
- Something wrong, man?

59
00:08:31,560 --> 00:08:33,516
You look a little whiter than usual.

60
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:36,670
My computer, it...

61
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:43,917
Ever have that feeling where you're
not sure if you're awake or still dreaming?

62
00:08:44,680 --> 00:08:47,319
All the time.
It's called mescaline.

63
00:08:47,800 --> 00:08:49,836
It's the only way to fly.

64
00:08:50,680 --> 00:08:53,069
It just sounds to me like you
need to unplug, man.

65
00:08:53,800 --> 00:08:55,756
Get some R and R?

66
00:08:56,120 --> 00:08:59,715
What do you think, Dujour?
Should we take him with us?

67
00:09:01,640 --> 00:09:02,789
Definitely.

68
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:06,037
No, I can't. I have work tomorrow.

69
00:09:06,560 --> 00:09:07,629
Come on.

70
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:10,394
It'll be fun. I promise.

71
00:09:16,640 --> 00:09:18,073
Yeah.

72
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:20,677
Sure. I'll go.

73
00:09:46,880 --> 00:09:48,154
Hello, Neo.

74
00:09:49,640 --> 00:09:52,996
- How do you know that name?
- I know a lot about you.

75
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:55,831
- Who are you?
- My name is Trinity.

76
00:09:56,760 --> 00:09:57,909
Trinity.

77
00:09:59,640 --> 00:10:02,677
The Trinity?
That cracked the IRS D-base?

78
00:10:02,920 --> 00:10:04,319
That was a long time ago.

79
00:10:04,560 --> 00:10:06,391
- Jesus.
- What?

80
00:10:06,840 --> 00:10:08,558
I just thought...

81
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:11,355
...you were a guy.

82
00:10:11,600 --> 00:10:12,999
Most guys do.

83
00:10:14,160 --> 00:10:16,276
That was you on my computer.

84
00:10:16,880 --> 00:10:17,949
How did you do that?

85
00:10:18,560 --> 00:10:21,154
Right now, all I can tell you...

86
00:10:21,760 --> 00:10:23,239
...is that you're in danger.

87
00:10:23,680 --> 00:10:25,989
- I brought you here to warn you.
- Of what?

88
00:10:26,560 --> 00:10:28,152
They're watching you, Neo.

89
00:10:28,720 --> 00:10:31,029
- Who is?
- Please just listen.

90
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:36,152
I know why you're here, Neo.

91
00:10:36,920 --> 00:10:38,797
I know what you've been doing.

92
00:10:39,040 --> 00:10:40,837
I know why you hardly sleep...

93
00:10:41,120 --> 00:10:44,112
...why you live alone and why,
night after night...

94
00:10:44,360 --> 00:10:46,590
...you sit at your computer.

95
00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:49,199
You're looking for him.

96
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:52,838
I know, because I was once
looking for the same thing.

97
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:55,356
And when he found me...

98
00:10:55,960 --> 00:10:58,918
...he told me I wasn't really
looking for him...

99
00:10:59,800 --> 00:11:01,472
...I was looking for an answer.

100
00:11:02,080 --> 00:11:05,072
It's the question that drives us, Neo.

101
00:11:05,720 --> 00:11:08,280
It's the question
that brought you here.

102
00:11:10,280 --> 00:11:11,599
You know the question...

103
00:11:11,840 --> 00:11:13,273
...just as I did.

104
00:11:14,760 --> 00:11:16,318
What is the Matrix?

105
00:11:16,560 --> 00:11:18,915
The answer is out there, Neo.

106
00:11:19,560 --> 00:11:21,471
It's looking for you.

107
00:11:22,240 --> 00:11:23,878
And it will find you...

108
00:11:24,120 --> 00:11:26,031
...if you want it to.

109
00:11:31,560 --> 00:11:32,549
Oh, Shit.

110
00:11:32,549 --> 00:11:34,789
Oh, Shit, shit.

111
00:11:44,640 --> 00:11:47,359
You have a problem with authority,
Mr. Anderson.

112
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:51,479
You believe that you are special,
that somehow the rules do not apply to you.

113
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:54,071
Obviously, you are mistaken.

114
00:11:56,920 --> 00:11:59,673
This company is one of the top
software companies in the world...

115
00:11:59,920 --> 00:12:03,151
...because every single employee understands
they are part of a whole.

116
00:12:03,400 --> 00:12:07,837
Thus, if an employee has a problem,
the company has a problem.

117
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:13,072
The time has come to make
a choice, Mr. Anderson.

118
00:12:13,920 --> 00:12:17,629
Either you choose to be at your desk
on time from this day forth...

119
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:20,708
...or you choose to find yourself another job.

120
00:12:21,560 --> 00:12:22,834
Do I make myself clear?

121
00:12:23,080 --> 00:12:25,389
Yes, Mr. Rhineheart.
Perfectly clear.

122
00:12:33,520 --> 00:12:35,431
Thomas Anderson?

123
00:12:36,520 --> 00:12:37,873
Yeah, that's me.

124
00:12:45,560 --> 00:12:46,675
Great.

125
00:12:48,040 --> 00:12:49,155
Have a nice day.

126
00:13:05,280 --> 00:13:08,477
{\i1}Hello, Neo. Do you know who this is?{\i}

127
00:13:10,640 --> 00:13:12,312
{\i1}- Morpheus.
- Yes.{\i}

128
00:13:12,560 --> 00:13:14,471
{\i1}I've been looking for you.
Neo.{\i}

129
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:17,757
{\i1}I don 't know if you're ready to see
what I want to show you.{\i}

130
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:21,037
{\i1}But unfortunately, you and I
have run out of time.{\i}

131
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:24,829
{\i1}They're coming for you Neo, and I don 't know
what they're going to do.{\i}

132
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:26,354
Who's coming for me?

133
00:13:26,600 --> 00:13:28,591
{\i1}Stand up and see for yourself.{\i}

134
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:31,513
{\i1}- What? Right now?
- Yes.{\i}

135
00:13:31,760 --> 00:13:32,954
{\i1}Now.{\i}

136
00:13:33,800 --> 00:13:35,597
{\i1}Do it slowly.{\i}

137
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,149
{\i1}The elevator.{\i}

138
00:13:41,840 --> 00:13:43,558
Oh, shit!
Yes.

139
00:13:48,040 --> 00:13:49,109
What the hell they want from me?

140
00:13:49,109 --> 00:13:52,556
{\i1}I don 't know. but If you don 't want
to find out, I suggest you get out of there.{\i}

141
00:13:52,556 --> 00:13:53,709
How?

142
00:13:53,709 --> 00:13:56,838
{\i1}I can guide you,
but you must do exactly as I say.{\i}

143
00:13:57,680 --> 00:13:59,591
{\i1}The cubicle across from you is empty.{\i}

144
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:04,636
{\i1}- But what if they...
- Go. Now.{\i}

145
00:14:11,120 --> 00:14:13,395
{\i1}Stay here for just a moment.{\i}

146
00:14:20,320 --> 00:14:22,959
{\i1}When I tell you,
go to the end of the row...{\i}

147
00:14:23,200 --> 00:14:25,077
{\i1}... to the office
at the end of the hall.{\i}

148
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:27,595
{\i1}Stay as low as you can.{\i}

149
00:14:29,880 --> 00:14:30,869
{\i1}Go. Now.{\i}

150
00:14:44,680 --> 00:14:48,070
{\i1}Good. Now, outside
there is a scaffold.{\i}

151
00:14:50,680 --> 00:14:52,910
{\i1}- How do you know all this?
- We don 't have time Neo.{\i}

152
00:14:53,160 --> 00:14:55,879
{\i1}To your left there's a window.
Go to it.{\i}

153
00:14:58,040 --> 00:14:59,519
{\i1}Open it.{\i}

154
00:15:00,320 --> 00:15:02,038
{\i1}Take the scaffold to the roof.{\i}

155
00:15:02,280 --> 00:15:04,748
No way! No way!
This is crazy!

156
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:07,275
{\i1}There are two ways
out of this building.{\i}

157
00:15:07,520 --> 00:15:11,149
{\i1}One is that scaffold.
The other is in their custody.{\i}

158
00:15:11,400 --> 00:15:14,472
{\i1}You take a chance either way.
I leave it to you.{\i}

159
00:15:17,920 --> 00:15:19,592
This is insane!

160
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:22,517
Why is this happening to me?

161
00:15:22,800 --> 00:15:24,358
What'd I do?

162
00:15:24,720 --> 00:15:27,359
I'm nobody.
I didn't do anything.

163
00:15:27,920 --> 00:15:29,319
I'm gonna die.

164
00:15:38,720 --> 00:15:39,709
Shit!

165
00:15:59,160 --> 00:16:00,229
Oh, shit!

166
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:06,718
I can't do this.

167
00:16:18,800 --> 00:16:19,835
Shit.

168
00:17:07,080 --> 00:17:11,710
As you can see, we've had our eye
on you for some time now, Mr. Anderson.

169
00:17:12,960 --> 00:17:15,520
It seems that you've been living...

170
00:17:15,760 --> 00:17:17,796
...two lives.

171
00:17:19,160 --> 00:17:21,549
In one life,
you're Thomas A. Anderson...

172
00:17:21,800 --> 00:17:24,997
...program writer for
a respectable software company.

173
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:29,151
You have a social security number.
You pay your taxes.

174
00:17:29,600 --> 00:17:30,794
And you...

175
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:35,790
...help your landlady
carry out her garbage.

176
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:41,192
The other life is lived in computers...

177
00:17:41,480 --> 00:17:44,313
...where you go by
the hacker alias "Neo"...

178
00:17:44,560 --> 00:17:49,156
...and are guilty of virtually every
computer crime we have a law for.

179
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:52,277
One of these lives...

180
00:17:52,520 --> 00:17:54,272
...has a future.

181
00:17:54,600 --> 00:17:56,511
And one of them does not.

182
00:18:00,080 --> 00:18:03,755
I'm going to be as forthcoming
as I can be, Mr. Anderson.

183
00:18:04,720 --> 00:18:05,994
You're here...

184
00:18:06,320 --> 00:18:08,470
...because we need your help.

185
00:18:11,960 --> 00:18:14,838
We know that you've been contacted
by a certain...

186
00:18:15,080 --> 00:18:16,798
...individual.

187
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:21,559
A man who calls himself "Morpheus."

188
00:18:22,520 --> 00:18:26,354
Whatever you think you know
about this man is irrelevant.

189
00:18:26,600 --> 00:18:28,909
He is considered by many authorities...

190
00:18:29,160 --> 00:18:32,072
...to be the most dangerous man alive.

191
00:18:34,720 --> 00:18:35,869
My colleagues...

192
00:18:36,280 --> 00:18:39,078
...believe that I am wasting
my time with you.

193
00:18:39,360 --> 00:18:42,636
But I believe you wish
to do the right thing.

194
00:18:42,920 --> 00:18:46,276
We're willing to wipe the slate clean...

195
00:18:46,640 --> 00:18:48,676
...give you a fresh start.

196
00:18:49,160 --> 00:18:51,958
Now, all we're asking in return
is your cooperation...

197
00:18:52,200 --> 00:18:55,556
...in bringing
a known terrorist to justice.

198
00:18:56,880 --> 00:18:58,074
Yeah.

199
00:18:59,320 --> 00:19:01,311
Well, that sounds like a really good deal.

200
00:19:02,880 --> 00:19:04,552
But I think I got a better one.

201
00:19:04,800 --> 00:19:06,233
How about...

202
00:19:06,640 --> 00:19:08,551
...I give you the finger...

203
00:19:11,040 --> 00:19:12,996
...and you give me my phone call.

204
00:19:15,080 --> 00:19:16,832
Mr. Anderson...

205
00:19:20,640 --> 00:19:21,834
...you disappoint me.

206
00:19:22,080 --> 00:19:24,594
You can't scare me
with this gestapo crap.

207
00:19:24,840 --> 00:19:26,159
I know my rights.

208
00:19:26,400 --> 00:19:27,833
I want my phone call.

209
00:19:28,400 --> 00:19:30,470
Tell me, Mr. Anderson...

210
00:19:31,320 --> 00:19:32,673
...what good is a phone call...

211
00:19:32,920 --> 00:19:36,356
...if you're unable to speak?

212
00:20:08,760 --> 00:20:10,876
You're going to help us,
Mr. Anderson...

213
00:20:11,560 --> 00:20:13,551
...whether you want to or not.

214
00:21:09,480 --> 00:21:12,597
{\i1}This line is tapped,
so I must be brief.{\i}

215
00:21:12,840 --> 00:21:16,958
{\i1}They got to you first, but they've
underestimated how important you are.{\i}

216
00:21:17,200 --> 00:21:18,952
{\i1}If they knew what I know...{\i}

217
00:21:19,200 --> 00:21:21,111
{\i1}... you would probably be dead.{\i}

218
00:21:22,080 --> 00:21:25,629
What are you talking about?
What........What is happening to me?

219
00:21:25,880 --> 00:21:30,510
{\i1}You are the One, Neo. You see you may have
spent the last few years...{\i}

220
00:21:30,760 --> 00:21:33,593
{\i1}... looking for me, but I've spent
my entire life...{\i}

221
00:21:33,840 --> 00:21:35,273
{\i1}... looking for you.{\i}

222
00:21:36,760 --> 00:21:38,830
{\i1}Now, do you still want to meet?{\i}

223
00:21:39,760 --> 00:21:42,513
{\i1}- Yes.
- Then go to the Adams Street bridge.{\i}

224
00:21:52,320 --> 00:21:53,469
Get in.

225
00:22:05,240 --> 00:22:08,710
- What the hell is this?
- It's necessary, Neo. For our protection.

226
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:11,030
- From what?
- From you.

227
00:22:12,520 --> 00:22:13,919
Take off your shirt.
WHAT.

228
00:22:14,240 --> 00:22:16,117
Stop the car.

229
00:22:19,600 --> 00:22:20,715
Listen to me, coppertop.

230
00:22:20,960 --> 00:22:22,871
We don't have time for 20 Questions.

231
00:22:23,360 --> 00:22:25,635
Right now, there's only one rule:

232
00:22:25,920 --> 00:22:27,194
Our way...

233
00:22:27,520 --> 00:22:28,555
...or the highway.

234
00:22:34,800 --> 00:22:35,869
Fine.

235
00:22:37,680 --> 00:22:40,035
Please, Neo, you have to trust me.

236
00:22:40,600 --> 00:22:43,114
- Why?
- Because you have been down there, Neo.

237
00:22:43,840 --> 00:22:44,989
You know that road.

238
00:22:45,960 --> 00:22:47,552
You know exactly where it ends.

239
00:22:49,640 --> 00:22:51,790
And I know that's
not where you want to be.

240
00:23:05,400 --> 00:23:06,879
Apoc, lights.

241
00:23:09,280 --> 00:23:11,350
Lie back.
Lift up your shirt.

242
00:23:13,200 --> 00:23:15,350
- What's that thing?
- We think You're bugged.

243
00:23:22,800 --> 00:23:24,199
Try and relax.

244
00:23:30,240 --> 00:23:31,355
Come on.

245
00:23:32,520 --> 00:23:34,476
Come on.

246
00:23:35,080 --> 00:23:37,036
It's on the move.

247
00:23:37,720 --> 00:23:38,869
Come on, you shit.

248
00:23:40,640 --> 00:23:42,631
- You're gonna lose it.
- No, I'm not.

249
00:23:42,631 --> 00:23:43,994
Clear!

250
00:23:52,240 --> 00:23:54,276
Jesus Christ!
That thing is real.

251
00:24:26,640 --> 00:24:27,914
This is it.

252
00:24:31,120 --> 00:24:33,475
Let me give you one piece of advice.

253
00:24:34,400 --> 00:24:35,992
Be honest.

254
00:24:37,520 --> 00:24:39,636
He knows more than you can imagine.

255
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:49,274
At last.

256
00:24:50,760 --> 00:24:51,795
Welcome, Neo.

257
00:24:52,960 --> 00:24:54,791
As you no doubt have guessed...

258
00:24:55,040 --> 00:24:56,234
...I am Morpheus.

259
00:24:57,240 --> 00:24:58,753
It's an honor to meet you.

260
00:24:59,200 --> 00:25:00,189
No...

261
00:25:00,760 --> 00:25:01,988
...the honor is mine.

262
00:25:02,880 --> 00:25:05,269
Please, come. Sit.

263
00:25:19,760 --> 00:25:21,318
I imagine...

264
00:25:21,720 --> 00:25:24,359
...that right now you're feeling
a bit like Alice...

265
00:25:26,000 --> 00:25:28,309
...tumbling down the rabbit hole?

266
00:25:29,200 --> 00:25:30,872
You could say that.

267
00:25:30,872 --> 00:25:33,554
I can see it in your eyes.

268
00:25:34,120 --> 00:25:37,271
You have the look of a man
who accepts what he sees...

269
00:25:37,520 --> 00:25:39,670
...because he's expecting to wake up.

270
00:25:41,040 --> 00:25:43,554
Ironically, this is not
far from the truth.

271
00:25:44,200 --> 00:25:46,589
Do you believe in fate, Neo?

272
00:25:46,880 --> 00:25:49,075
- No.
- Why not?

273
00:25:49,320 --> 00:25:51,993
Because I don't like the idea that
I'm not in control of my life.

274
00:25:53,040 --> 00:25:56,999
I know exactly what you mean.

275
00:26:00,360 --> 00:26:02,635
Let me tell you why you're here.

276
00:26:03,640 --> 00:26:05,119
You're here because
You know something.

277
00:26:05,640 --> 00:26:07,198
What you know,
you can't explain.

278
00:26:07,680 --> 00:26:09,193
But you feel it.

279
00:26:09,760 --> 00:26:11,591
You felt it your entire life.

280
00:26:12,160 --> 00:26:16,153
Is there something's wrong with the world.
You don't know what it is, but it's there.

281
00:26:16,640 --> 00:26:18,756
Like a splinter in your mind...

282
00:26:19,000 --> 00:26:20,797
...driving you mad.

283
00:26:21,680 --> 00:26:24,319
It is this feeling
that has brought you to me.

284
00:26:26,760 --> 00:26:28,512
Do you know what
I'm talking about?

285
00:26:30,280 --> 00:26:31,554
The Matrix?

286
00:26:33,960 --> 00:26:35,552
Do you want to know...

287
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:37,911
...what it is?

288
00:26:40,200 --> 00:26:41,997
The Matrix is everywhere.

289
00:26:42,240 --> 00:26:43,878
It is all around us.

290
00:26:44,120 --> 00:26:45,997
Even now, in this very room.

291
00:26:46,800 --> 00:26:48,916
You can see it when you
look out your window...

292
00:26:49,160 --> 00:26:51,390
...or when you turn on your television.

293
00:26:51,800 --> 00:26:54,234
You can feel it when you go to work...

294
00:26:55,720 --> 00:26:57,312
...when you go to church...

295
00:26:57,720 --> 00:26:59,711
...when you pay your taxes.

296
00:27:00,800 --> 00:27:03,598
It is the world that has been
pulled over your eyes...

297
00:27:03,840 --> 00:27:05,353
...to blind you from the truth.

298
00:27:07,480 --> 00:27:08,674
What truth?

299
00:27:12,760 --> 00:27:14,600
That you are a slave, Neo.

300
00:27:15,680 --> 00:27:17,875
Like everyone else,
you were born into bondage...

301
00:27:18,120 --> 00:27:22,591
...born into a prison that you cannot
smell or taste or touch.

302
00:27:22,880 --> 00:27:24,108
A prison...

303
00:27:24,360 --> 00:27:25,475
...for your mind.

304
00:27:32,160 --> 00:27:34,390
Unfortunately, no one can be...

305
00:27:34,720 --> 00:27:36,995
...told what the Matrix is.

306
00:27:40,320 --> 00:27:42,117
You have to see it for yourself.

307
00:27:51,240 --> 00:27:53,435
This is your last chance.

308
00:27:53,680 --> 00:27:55,910
After this, there is no turning back.

309
00:27:56,360 --> 00:27:57,793
You take the blue pill...

310
00:27:58,080 --> 00:28:00,992
...the story ends, you wake up
in your bed and believe...

311
00:28:01,240 --> 00:28:02,958
...whatever you want to believe.

312
00:28:03,200 --> 00:28:04,474
You take the red pill...

313
00:28:04,720 --> 00:28:06,597
...you stay in Wonderland...

314
00:28:07,080 --> 00:28:09,674
...and I show you how deep
the rabbit hole goes.

315
00:28:19,160 --> 00:28:20,309
Remember...

316
00:28:21,120 --> 00:28:24,032
...all I'm offering is the truth.
Nothing more.

317
00:28:37,760 --> 00:28:39,034
Follow me.

318
00:28:41,480 --> 00:28:43,072
Apoc, are we on-line?

319
00:28:43,320 --> 00:28:44,639
Almost.

320
00:28:47,840 --> 00:28:49,796
Time is always against us.

321
00:28:50,160 --> 00:28:51,593
Please take a seat there.

322
00:29:09,040 --> 00:29:10,678
You did all this?

323
00:29:14,640 --> 00:29:16,551
The pill you took is
part of a trace program.

324
00:29:17,280 --> 00:29:21,717
It's designed to disrupts your Input-Output carrier
signals, so we can pinpoint your location.

325
00:29:22,240 --> 00:29:23,229
What does that mean?

326
00:29:23,800 --> 00:29:25,870
It means buckle your
seat belt, Dorothy...

327
00:29:26,200 --> 00:29:27,474
...because Kansas...

328
00:29:27,720 --> 00:29:28,709
...is going bye-bye.

329
00:30:05,080 --> 00:30:06,399
Did you..

330
00:30:16,960 --> 00:30:20,873
Have you ever had a dream, Neo,
that you were so sure was real?

331
00:30:22,280 --> 00:30:24,748
What if you were unable
to wake from that dream?

332
00:30:25,000 --> 00:30:27,389
How would you know the difference
between the dream world...

333
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:29,353
...and the real world?

334
00:30:30,920 --> 00:30:33,195
- This can't be.
- Be what?

335
00:30:33,880 --> 00:30:35,313
Be real?

336
00:30:39,120 --> 00:30:40,800
It's going into replication.
Apoc.

337
00:30:40,800 --> 00:30:43,360
- Still nothing.
- It's cold.

338
00:30:43,600 --> 00:30:44,919
It's cold!

339
00:30:48,640 --> 00:30:50,232
Tank, we are going to need a signal soon.

340
00:30:51,720 --> 00:30:54,234
- I got a fibrillation.
- Apoc, location.

341
00:30:54,480 --> 00:30:55,879
Targeting almost there.

342
00:30:59,040 --> 00:31:00,393
He's going into arrest.

343
00:31:00,640 --> 00:31:03,029
- Lock. I got him!
- Now, Tank, now!

344
00:33:53,040 --> 00:33:54,075
Welcome...

345
00:33:54,400 --> 00:33:56,231
...to the real world.

346
00:33:57,600 --> 00:33:59,352
We've done it, Trinity.

347
00:33:59,600 --> 00:34:01,079
We found him.

348
00:34:01,320 --> 00:34:03,993
- I hope you're right.
- I don't have to hope.

349
00:34:04,560 --> 00:34:06,073
I know it.

350
00:34:11,040 --> 00:34:12,029
Am I dead?

351
00:34:12,520 --> 00:34:14,590
Far from it.

352
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:29,353
He still needs a lot of work.

353
00:34:30,840 --> 00:34:31,875
What are you doing?

354
00:34:32,120 --> 00:34:34,236
Your muscles have atrophied.
We're rebuilding them.

355
00:34:34,800 --> 00:34:36,279
Why do my eyes hurt?

356
00:34:36,960 --> 00:34:38,757
You've never used them before.

357
00:34:42,560 --> 00:34:45,199
Rest, Neo. The answers are coming.

358
00:35:56,720 --> 00:35:58,233
Morpheus, what's happened to me?

359
00:35:58,960 --> 00:36:02,669
- What is this place?
- More important than "what" is "when."

360
00:36:03,360 --> 00:36:06,318
- When?
- You believe it's the year 1999...

361
00:36:06,560 --> 00:36:08,710
...when in fact, it's closer to 2199.

362
00:36:09,800 --> 00:36:12,439
I can't tell you exactly
what year it is...

363
00:36:12,680 --> 00:36:14,238
...because we honestly don't know.

364
00:36:14,720 --> 00:36:17,439
There's nothing I can say
that will explain it for you, Neo.

365
00:36:17,680 --> 00:36:18,795
Come with me.

366
00:36:19,080 --> 00:36:20,308
See for yourself.

367
00:36:20,840 --> 00:36:22,512
This is my ship.

368
00:36:22,800 --> 00:36:25,598
{\i1}The Nebuchadnezzar.
It's a hovercraft.{\i}

369
00:36:28,320 --> 00:36:29,992
This is the main deck.

370
00:36:35,600 --> 00:36:36,715
This is the core...

371
00:36:39,120 --> 00:36:42,715
...where we broadcast our pirate signal
and hack into the Matrix.

372
00:36:45,960 --> 00:36:48,997
Most of my crew you already know.

373
00:36:53,800 --> 00:36:55,153
This is Apoc...

374
00:36:55,920 --> 00:36:57,194
...Switch...

375
00:36:58,720 --> 00:36:59,835
...and Cypher.
---Hi.

376
00:37:00,080 --> 00:37:03,629
The ones you don't know:
Tank and his big brother, Dozer.

377
00:37:04,480 --> 00:37:06,789
The little one behind you is Mouse.

378
00:37:10,960 --> 00:37:14,700
You wanted to know
what the Matrix is, Neo.?

379
00:37:15,080 --> 00:37:16,229
Trinity.

380
00:37:36,400 --> 00:37:37,913
Try to relax.

381
00:37:42,600 --> 00:37:44,352
This will feel a little weird.

382
00:37:55,840 --> 00:37:56,955
This...

383
00:37:57,320 --> 00:37:58,958
...is the Construct.

384
00:37:59,360 --> 00:38:01,396
It's our loading program.

385
00:38:01,640 --> 00:38:03,995
We can load anything, from clothing...

386
00:38:04,240 --> 00:38:05,559
...to equipment...

387
00:38:05,840 --> 00:38:07,114
...weapons...

388
00:38:07,720 --> 00:38:09,472
...training simulations...

389
00:38:09,840 --> 00:38:12,274
...anything we need.

390
00:38:14,960 --> 00:38:17,269
Right now we're inside
a computer program?

391
00:38:17,560 --> 00:38:19,391
Is it really so hard to believe?

392
00:38:19,880 --> 00:38:22,394
Your clothes are different.
The plugs in your arms and head are gone.

393
00:38:23,560 --> 00:38:25,551
Your hair has changed.

394
00:38:25,920 --> 00:38:29,117
Your appearance now is what we call
"residual self-image."

395
00:38:29,800 --> 00:38:32,314
It is the mental projection
of your digital self.

396
00:38:37,960 --> 00:38:39,029
This isn't real?

397
00:38:39,280 --> 00:38:40,759
What is "real"?

398
00:38:41,120 --> 00:38:43,270
How do you define "real"?

399
00:38:43,560 --> 00:38:45,391
If you're talking about
what you can feel...

400
00:38:45,640 --> 00:38:47,949
...what you can smell, what you
can taste and see...

401
00:38:48,200 --> 00:38:51,909
...then "real" is simply electrical
signals interpreted by your brain.

402
00:38:55,920 --> 00:38:58,229
This is the world that you know.

403
00:38:59,600 --> 00:39:02,512
The world as it was at the end
of the 20th century.

404
00:39:04,800 --> 00:39:08,952
It exists now only as part of
a neural-interactive simulation...

405
00:39:09,200 --> 00:39:10,394
...that we call the Matrix.

406
00:39:14,760 --> 00:39:17,479
You've been living
in a dream world, Neo.

407
00:39:18,400 --> 00:39:19,469
This is the world...

408
00:39:19,760 --> 00:39:21,478
...as it exists today.

409
00:39:33,960 --> 00:39:36,793
Welcome to "the desert...

410
00:39:37,640 --> 00:39:39,153
...of the real."

411
00:39:42,400 --> 00:39:44,675
We have only bits and pieces
of information.

412
00:39:44,920 --> 00:39:48,549
But what we know for certain is that at
some point in the early 21st century...

413
00:39:48,800 --> 00:39:51,917
...all of mankind was united
in celebration.

414
00:39:52,160 --> 00:39:57,480
We marveled at our own magnificence
as we gave birth to AI.

415
00:39:57,480 --> 00:39:58,549
AI [=Artificial Intelligence]

416
00:39:59,560 --> 00:40:00,879
You mean artificial intelligence.

417
00:40:01,120 --> 00:40:05,352
A singular consciousness that spawned
an entire race of machines.

418
00:40:06,160 --> 00:40:09,470
We don't know who struck first,
us or them.

419
00:40:09,880 --> 00:40:12,952
But we know that it was us
that scorched the sky.

420
00:40:14,560 --> 00:40:16,630
At the time they were dependent
on solar power...

421
00:40:16,880 --> 00:40:20,077
...and it was believed that
they would be unable to survive...

422
00:40:20,400 --> 00:40:23,756
...without an energy sources
as abundant as the sun.

423
00:40:24,000 --> 00:40:28,676
Throughout human history, we have been
dependent on machines to survive.

424
00:40:30,080 --> 00:40:34,119
Fate, it seems, is not
without a sense of irony.

425
00:40:37,200 --> 00:40:41,432
The human body generates more
bioelectricity than a 120-volt battery.

426
00:40:41,680 --> 00:40:45,639
And over 25,000 BTUs of body heat.

427
00:40:47,480 --> 00:40:49,550
Combined with a form of fusion...

428
00:40:49,880 --> 00:40:54,510
...the machines had found all the energy
they would ever need.

429
00:40:58,400 --> 00:41:01,995
There are fields, Neo. endless fields...

430
00:41:02,240 --> 00:41:05,357
...where human beings
are no longer born.

431
00:41:06,040 --> 00:41:07,792
We are grown.

432
00:41:13,600 --> 00:41:16,068
For the longest time,
I wouldn't believe it.

433
00:41:16,320 --> 00:41:18,880
And then I saw the fields
with my own eyes...

434
00:41:20,160 --> 00:41:21,718
...watched them liquefy the dead...

435
00:41:21,960 --> 00:41:25,157
...so they could be fed intravenously
to the living.

436
00:41:25,680 --> 00:41:29,753
And standing there,
facing the pure, horrifying precision...

437
00:41:30,000 --> 00:41:32,798
...I came to realize
the obviousness of the truth.

438
00:41:35,320 --> 00:41:37,038
What is the Matrix?

439
00:41:38,200 --> 00:41:39,189
Control.

440
00:41:40,520 --> 00:41:43,751
The Matrix is a computer-generated
dream world...

441
00:41:44,520 --> 00:41:47,478
...built to keep us under control...

442
00:41:48,600 --> 00:41:51,637
...in order to change a human being...

443
00:41:52,240 --> 00:41:53,355
...into this.

444
00:41:54,680 --> 00:41:55,749
No.

445
00:41:57,320 --> 00:41:58,833
I don't believe it.

446
00:41:59,200 --> 00:42:00,349
It's not possible.

447
00:42:00,920 --> 00:42:05,311
I didn't say it would be easy, Neo.
I just said it would be the truth.

448
00:42:05,560 --> 00:42:07,073
Stop!

449
00:42:07,320 --> 00:42:08,469
Let me out!

450
00:42:09,160 --> 00:42:10,991
Let me out! I want out!

451
00:42:12,880 --> 00:42:15,440
- Easy, Neo. Easy.
- Get this thing out of me.

452
00:42:15,680 --> 00:42:17,272
Get this thing out of me!

453
00:42:19,000 --> 00:42:20,433
Don't touch me!
Stay away from me!

454
00:42:20,433 --> 00:42:22,238
Stay away from me!

455
00:42:22,640 --> 00:42:24,073
I don't believe it.

456
00:42:24,760 --> 00:42:25,909
I don't believe it.

457
00:42:26,160 --> 00:42:27,673
I don't believe it.

458
00:42:27,673 --> 00:42:31,196
- He's gonna pop.
- Breathe, Neo. Just breathe.

459
00:42:48,840 --> 00:42:50,558
I can't go back, can I?

460
00:42:51,120 --> 00:42:52,394
No.

461
00:42:53,520 --> 00:42:54,669
But if you could...

462
00:42:55,480 --> 00:42:56,913
...would you really want to?

463
00:42:59,320 --> 00:43:00,673
I feel I owe you an apology.

464
00:43:01,200 --> 00:43:02,519
We have a rule.

465
00:43:02,960 --> 00:43:06,191
We never free a mind
once it's reached a certain age.

466
00:43:06,440 --> 00:43:09,591
It's dangerous.
The mind has trouble letting go.

467
00:43:09,840 --> 00:43:12,035
I've seen it before, and I'm sorry.

468
00:43:13,040 --> 00:43:15,031
I did what I did because...

469
00:43:15,720 --> 00:43:17,119
...I had to.

470
00:43:25,200 --> 00:43:29,113
When the Matrix was first built,
there was a man born inside...

471
00:43:29,600 --> 00:43:33,229
...who had the ability
to change whatever he wanted...

472
00:43:33,600 --> 00:43:36,398
...to remake the Matrix as he saw fit.

473
00:43:38,080 --> 00:43:41,390
It was he who freed the first of us...

474
00:43:42,240 --> 00:43:43,798
...taught us the truth.

475
00:43:45,200 --> 00:43:48,158
As long as the Matrix exists...

476
00:43:48,480 --> 00:43:50,471
...the human race will never be free.

477
00:43:54,520 --> 00:43:55,999
After he died...

478
00:43:56,720 --> 00:43:59,314
...the Oracle prophesied his return...

479
00:43:59,840 --> 00:44:02,912
...and that his coming would hail
the destruction of the Matrix...

480
00:44:03,160 --> 00:44:04,752
...end the war...

481
00:44:05,080 --> 00:44:06,229
...bring freedom to our people.

482
00:44:07,560 --> 00:44:11,997
That is why there are those of us who has
spent our entire lives searching the Matrix...

483
00:44:12,320 --> 00:44:13,833
...looking for him.

484
00:44:16,160 --> 00:44:18,151
I did what I did because...

485
00:44:19,720 --> 00:44:21,756
...I believe that search is over.

486
00:44:26,640 --> 00:44:27,993
Get some rest.

487
00:44:28,600 --> 00:44:30,318
You're going to need it.

488
00:44:32,960 --> 00:44:34,837
For what?

489
00:44:36,880 --> 00:44:37,995
Your training.

490
00:44:55,560 --> 00:44:57,198
Morning. Did you sleep?

491
00:44:58,040 --> 00:44:59,189
You will tonight.

492
00:44:59,560 --> 00:45:01,039
I guarantee it.

493
00:45:02,480 --> 00:45:04,311
I'm Tank. I'll be your operator.

494
00:45:04,760 --> 00:45:07,069
- You don't have any...
- Holes? Nope.

495
00:45:07,960 --> 00:45:12,476
Me and my brother, Dozer, we are both 100% pure,
old-fashioned, homegrown human.

496
00:45:12,720 --> 00:45:13,869
Born free right here...

497
00:45:14,400 --> 00:45:15,674
...in the real world.

498
00:45:15,920 --> 00:45:17,512
Genuine child of Zion.

499
00:45:18,320 --> 00:45:20,675
- Zion?
- If the war was over tomorrow...

500
00:45:20,920 --> 00:45:22,273
...Zion's where the party would be.

501
00:45:22,760 --> 00:45:23,988
It's a city?

502
00:45:24,240 --> 00:45:27,277
The last human city.
The only place we have left.

503
00:45:28,800 --> 00:45:29,994
Where is it?

504
00:45:31,320 --> 00:45:32,639
Deep underground...

505
00:45:32,880 --> 00:45:34,950
...near the Earth's core,
where it's still warm.

506
00:45:36,520 --> 00:45:38,317
You live long enough,
you might even see it.

507
00:45:40,480 --> 00:45:45,110
Goddamn! I gotta tell you, I'm really excited
to see what you're capable of...

508
00:45:45,360 --> 00:45:47,032
...if Morpheus is right and all.

509
00:45:47,520 --> 00:45:50,159
We're not supposed to
talk about this, but...

510
00:45:50,400 --> 00:45:51,753
...if you are...

511
00:45:52,800 --> 00:45:54,711
...it's a very exciting time.

512
00:45:55,720 --> 00:45:58,314
We got a lot to do.
We gotta get to it.

513
00:46:02,080 --> 00:46:04,878
We're supposed to start
with these operation programs first.

514
00:46:05,840 --> 00:46:09,150
That's major boring shit.
Let's do something little more fun.

515
00:46:09,480 --> 00:46:10,913
How about...

516
00:46:12,400 --> 00:46:14,072
...combat training?

517
00:46:19,880 --> 00:46:21,279
"Jujitsu"?

518
00:46:22,120 --> 00:46:23,712
I'm going to learn jujitsu?

519
00:46:34,600 --> 00:46:35,749
Holy shit!

520
00:46:36,000 --> 00:46:38,230
"Hey, Mikey, I think he likes it."

521
00:46:38,560 --> 00:46:39,788
How about some more?

522
00:46:40,040 --> 00:46:41,268
Hell, yes.

523
00:46:43,200 --> 00:46:44,269
Hell, yeah.

524
00:46:55,880 --> 00:46:56,995
How is he?

525
00:46:57,240 --> 00:46:59,356
Ten hours straight.
He's a machine.

526
00:47:10,080 --> 00:47:11,399
I know kung fu.

527
00:47:13,000 --> 00:47:13,989
Show me.

528
00:47:15,680 --> 00:47:17,352
This is a sparring program...

529
00:47:17,600 --> 00:47:20,273
...similar to the programmed reality
of the Matrix.

530
00:47:20,520 --> 00:47:22,750
It has the same basic rules.
Rules like gravity.

531
00:47:23,000 --> 00:47:26,310
What you must learn is that these rules are no
different than the rules of a computer system.

532
00:47:26,840 --> 00:47:28,273
Some of them can be bent.

533
00:47:28,480 --> 00:47:30,835
Others can be broken.

534
00:47:31,200 --> 00:47:32,394
Understand?

535
00:47:33,640 --> 00:47:36,074
Then hit me, if you can.

536
00:48:13,360 --> 00:48:14,475
Good!

537
00:48:15,200 --> 00:48:16,315
Adaptation.

538
00:48:16,600 --> 00:48:17,749
Improvisation.

539
00:48:18,040 --> 00:48:19,314
But your weakness...

540
00:48:19,560 --> 00:48:20,879
...is not your technique.

541
00:48:27,560 --> 00:48:29,551
Morpheus is fighting Neo.

542
00:49:38,880 --> 00:49:39,995
How did I beat you?

543
00:49:46,320 --> 00:49:47,355
You're too fast.

544
00:49:47,880 --> 00:49:49,154
Do you believe that...

545
00:49:49,520 --> 00:49:51,909
...my being stronger or faster...

546
00:49:52,160 --> 00:49:55,675
...has anything to do
with my muscles in this place?

547
00:49:59,560 --> 00:50:01,999
You think that's air you're breathing now.

548
00:50:14,240 --> 00:50:15,389
Again!

549
00:50:26,400 --> 00:50:28,709
Jesus Christ, he's fast!

550
00:50:28,960 --> 00:50:32,076
Take a look. His neuro-kinetics
are way above normal.

551
00:50:36,320 --> 00:50:37,719
What are you waiting for?

552
00:50:37,960 --> 00:50:39,837
You're faster than this.

553
00:50:41,960 --> 00:50:44,076
Don't think you are.

554
00:50:44,320 --> 00:50:45,912
Know you are.

555
00:50:55,880 --> 00:50:58,599
Come on! Stop trying to hit me,
and hit me!

556
00:51:08,080 --> 00:51:09,752
I don't believe it.

557
00:51:11,240 --> 00:51:13,276
I know what you're trying to do.

558
00:51:14,880 --> 00:51:16,950
I'm trying to free your mind, Neo.

559
00:51:17,280 --> 00:51:19,271
But I can only show you the door.

560
00:51:19,840 --> 00:51:21,637
You are the one that have to walk through it.

561
00:51:23,880 --> 00:51:25,916
Tank, load the jump program.

562
00:51:37,040 --> 00:51:39,634
You have to let it all go, Neo.
Fear...

563
00:51:40,160 --> 00:51:42,230
...doubt and disbelief.

564
00:51:43,360 --> 00:51:45,954
Free your mind.

565
00:52:01,480 --> 00:52:03,118
Okey-dokey.

566
00:52:05,120 --> 00:52:06,235
Free my mind.

567
00:52:06,680 --> 00:52:07,749
What if he makes it?

568
00:52:08,000 --> 00:52:10,594
- No one's ever made their first jump.
- That I know. I Know.

569
00:52:11,880 --> 00:52:14,235
- But what if he does?
- He won't.

570
00:52:14,720 --> 00:52:15,835
Come on.

571
00:52:16,080 --> 00:52:17,195
All right.

572
00:52:17,640 --> 00:52:19,596
No problem. Free my mind.

573
00:52:20,360 --> 00:52:23,033
Free my mind. No problem. Right.

574
00:52:41,640 --> 00:52:43,232
What does that mean?

575
00:52:43,600 --> 00:52:45,352
It doesn't mean anything.

576
00:52:45,920 --> 00:52:48,388
Everybody falls the first time.

577
00:52:48,840 --> 00:52:50,068
Right, Trin?

578
00:53:09,920 --> 00:53:12,434
- I thought it wasn't real.
- Your mind makes it real.

579
00:53:15,560 --> 00:53:17,710
If you're killed in the Matrix...

580
00:53:17,710 --> 00:53:18,869
...you die here?

581
00:53:19,480 --> 00:53:21,835
The body cannot live without the mind.

582
00:53:51,080 --> 00:53:54,311
I don't remember you ever
bringing me dinner.

583
00:53:57,280 --> 00:53:59,999
There is something about him,
isn't there?

584
00:54:00,600 --> 00:54:02,158
Don't tell me you're a believer now?

585
00:54:03,120 --> 00:54:04,269
I just keep wondering...

586
00:54:04,520 --> 00:54:08,035
...if Morpheus is so sure,
why he isn't taking him to see the Oracle?

587
00:54:08,920 --> 00:54:11,718
Morpheus will take him
when he's ready.

588
00:54:21,120 --> 00:54:22,599
The Matrix is a system, Neo.

589
00:54:24,280 --> 00:54:25,508
That system is our enemy.

590
00:54:26,120 --> 00:54:28,350
But when you're inside,
You look around, what do you see?

591
00:54:28,600 --> 00:54:32,229
Businessmen, teachers,
lawyers, carpenters.

592
00:54:32,680 --> 00:54:35,148
The very minds of the people
we are trying to save.

593
00:54:35,400 --> 00:54:38,233
But until we do, these people are
still a part of that system...

594
00:54:38,480 --> 00:54:41,631
...and that makes them our enemy.
You have to understand...

595
00:54:41,880 --> 00:54:45,077
...most of these people are not
ready to be unplugged.

596
00:54:45,320 --> 00:54:46,833
And many of them are so inert...

597
00:54:47,080 --> 00:54:49,389
...so hopelessly dependent
on the system...

598
00:54:49,640 --> 00:54:52,234
...that they will fight to protect it.

599
00:54:53,680 --> 00:54:57,275
Were you listening to me Neo or were you
looking at the woman in the red dress?

600
00:54:57,275 --> 00:54:59,109
I was.....
Look again.

601
00:55:00,320 --> 00:55:01,355
Freeze it.

602
00:55:07,720 --> 00:55:09,999
This isn't the Matrix?
No.

603
00:55:11,000 --> 00:55:14,675
It's another training program
designed to teach you one thing:

604
00:55:15,280 --> 00:55:17,589
If you are not one of us,
you are one of them.

605
00:55:18,120 --> 00:55:20,793
- What are they?
- Sentient programs.

606
00:55:21,520 --> 00:55:25,638
They can move in and out of any software
still hardwired to their system.

607
00:55:26,000 --> 00:55:29,231
That means that anyone
we haven't unplugged...

608
00:55:29,560 --> 00:55:30,834
...is potentially an agent.

609
00:55:31,760 --> 00:55:33,512
Inside the Matrix...

610
00:55:34,080 --> 00:55:35,718
...they are everyone...

611
00:55:36,040 --> 00:55:37,678
...and they are no one.

612
00:55:37,920 --> 00:55:40,912
We are survived by hiding from them
by running from them...

613
00:55:41,160 --> 00:55:42,718
...but they are the gatekeepers.

614
00:55:42,960 --> 00:55:45,793
They're guarding all the doors.
They are holding all the keys, which means that

615
00:55:46,040 --> 00:55:48,759
Sooner or later, someone is going
to have to fight them.

616
00:55:48,759 --> 00:55:50,069
Someone?

617
00:55:50,400 --> 00:55:51,753
I won't lie to you, Neo.

618
00:55:52,200 --> 00:55:56,830
Every single man or woman who has stood their
ground. Everyone who has fought an agent has died.

619
00:55:57,080 --> 00:55:59,355
But where they have failed,
you will succeed.

620
00:55:59,560 --> 00:56:00,549
Why?

621
00:56:00,800 --> 00:56:02,995
I've seen an agent punch
through a concrete wall.

622
00:56:03,240 --> 00:56:06,676
Men have emptied entire clips at them
and hit nothing but air.

623
00:56:06,920 --> 00:56:11,357
Yet their strength and their speed are still
based in a world it is built on rules.

624
00:56:11,600 --> 00:56:12,669
Because of that...

625
00:56:12,920 --> 00:56:16,151
...they will never be as strong
or as fast as you can be.

626
00:56:20,280 --> 00:56:22,077
What are you trying to tell me?

627
00:56:22,760 --> 00:56:24,159
That I can dodge bullets?

628
00:56:26,080 --> 00:56:27,399
No, Neo.

629
00:56:27,880 --> 00:56:30,678
I'm trying to tell you
that when you're ready...

630
00:56:31,520 --> 00:56:32,839
...you won't have to.

631
00:56:36,960 --> 00:56:37,949
{\i1}We got trouble.{\i}

632
00:56:56,080 --> 00:56:59,435
- Did Zion send the warning?
- No, another ship.

633
00:57:01,560 --> 00:57:02,788
Shit.

634
00:57:03,040 --> 00:57:05,793
- Squiddy's sweeping in quick.
- Squiddy?

635
00:57:06,000 --> 00:57:09,072
A sentinel. A killing machine
designed for one thing.

636
00:57:09,320 --> 00:57:10,469
Search and destroy.

637
00:57:11,760 --> 00:57:12,999
Set her down right over there.

638
00:57:33,800 --> 00:57:35,836
How are we doing, Tank?

639
00:57:43,080 --> 00:57:44,195
Power off-line.

640
00:57:44,680 --> 00:57:46,591
EMP armed...

641
00:57:46,591 --> 00:57:48,557
...and ready.
- EMP?

642
00:57:48,840 --> 00:57:50,637
Electromagnetic pulse.

643
00:57:50,880 --> 00:57:53,633
Disables any electrical system
in the blast radius.

644
00:57:53,880 --> 00:57:56,996
It's the only weapon we have
against the machines.

645
00:58:01,560 --> 00:58:04,999
- Where are we?
- Their old service and waste systems.

646
00:58:05,840 --> 00:58:06,829
Sewers.

647
00:58:07,040 --> 00:58:09,634
There used to be cities
that spanned hundreds of miles.

648
00:58:10,120 --> 00:58:11,951
Now these sewers are
all that's left of them.

649
00:58:12,200 --> 00:58:13,474
Quiet.

650
00:58:55,560 --> 00:58:57,630
You scared the bejesus out of me.

651
00:58:58,680 --> 00:59:00,511
- Sorry.
- It's okay.

652
00:59:03,320 --> 00:59:06,880
- Is that..?
- The Matrix. YEAH.

653
00:59:08,920 --> 00:59:11,957
- Do you always look at it encoded?
- Well, you have to.

654
00:59:12,200 --> 00:59:15,158
The image translators work
for the construct program.

655
00:59:15,400 --> 00:59:18,676
But there's way too much information
to decode the Matrix.

656
00:59:18,920 --> 00:59:21,753
You get used to it.
I don't even see the code.

657
00:59:22,000 --> 00:59:25,276
All I see is blonde, brunette, redhead.

658
00:59:26,400 --> 00:59:27,719
Do you...

659
00:59:28,000 --> 00:59:29,035
...want a drink?

660
00:59:29,280 --> 00:59:30,269
Sure.

661
00:59:33,680 --> 00:59:35,079
You know...

662
00:59:35,960 --> 00:59:37,439
...I know what you're thinking.

663
00:59:37,680 --> 00:59:39,716
Because right now I'm thinking
the same thing.

664
00:59:40,000 --> 00:59:43,197
Actually, I've been thinking it
ever since I got here.

665
00:59:45,040 --> 00:59:47,918
Why, oh, why didn't I take
the blue pill?

666
00:59:59,800 --> 01:00:01,631
Good shit, huh?

667
01:00:01,960 --> 01:00:03,109
Dozer makes it.

668
01:00:03,560 --> 01:00:04,675
It's good for two things:

669
01:00:04,920 --> 01:00:07,878
Degreasing engines and
killing brain cells.

670
01:00:08,840 --> 01:00:10,956
So can I ask you something?

671
01:00:13,840 --> 01:00:15,398
Did he tell you why he did it?

672
01:00:17,920 --> 01:00:19,672
Why you're here?

673
01:00:23,200 --> 01:00:24,872
Jesus!

674
01:00:26,040 --> 01:00:27,871
What a mind job.

675
01:00:29,240 --> 01:00:31,913
So you're here to save the world.

676
01:00:33,360 --> 01:00:35,351
What do you say
to something like that?

677
01:00:40,320 --> 01:00:41,639
A little piece of advice.

678
01:00:43,360 --> 01:00:44,713
You see an agent...

679
01:00:45,040 --> 01:00:47,235
...you do what we do:

680
01:00:47,560 --> 01:00:49,039
Run.

681
01:00:49,360 --> 01:00:51,032
You run your ass off.

682
01:00:58,000 --> 01:00:59,638
Thanks for the drink.

683
01:01:04,160 --> 01:01:05,275
Sweet dreams.

684
01:01:09,120 --> 01:01:12,396
Do we have a deal, Mr. Reagan?

685
01:01:13,040 --> 01:01:14,109
You know...

686
01:01:15,480 --> 01:01:17,835
...I know this steak doesn't exist.

687
01:01:18,800 --> 01:01:21,439
I know that when I put it
in my mouth...

688
01:01:21,680 --> 01:01:24,638
...the Matrix is telling my brain
that it is...

689
01:01:24,920 --> 01:01:25,989
...juicy...

690
01:01:26,280 --> 01:01:27,918
...and delicious.

691
01:01:30,720 --> 01:01:31,914
After nine years...

692
01:01:32,920 --> 01:01:34,399
...you know what I realize?

693
01:01:41,920 --> 01:01:43,069
Ignorance is bliss.

694
01:01:47,920 --> 01:01:49,672
Then we have a deal.

695
01:01:52,080 --> 01:01:53,911
I don't want to remember nothing.

696
01:01:54,160 --> 01:01:56,594
Nothing. You understand?

697
01:02:00,480 --> 01:02:02,198
And I want to be rich.

698
01:02:03,480 --> 01:02:06,074
You know, someone important.

699
01:02:07,520 --> 01:02:08,589
Like an actor.

700
01:02:09,760 --> 01:02:12,752
Whatever you want, Mr. Reagan.

701
01:02:14,840 --> 01:02:16,319
Okay.

702
01:02:16,680 --> 01:02:18,989
You get my body
back in a power plant...

703
01:02:19,360 --> 01:02:21,032
...reinsert me into the Matrix...

704
01:02:21,360 --> 01:02:22,713
...I'll get you what you want.

705
01:02:22,960 --> 01:02:24,871
Access codes to the Zion mainframe.

706
01:02:25,120 --> 01:02:27,190
No. I told you, I don't know them.

707
01:02:30,040 --> 01:02:31,951
I can get you the man who does.

708
01:02:32,680 --> 01:02:34,398
Morpheus.

709
01:02:44,080 --> 01:02:47,390
Here you go, buddy.
Breakfast of champions.

710
01:02:48,680 --> 01:02:51,353
If you close your eyes, it almost feels
like you're eating runny eggs.

711
01:02:51,600 --> 01:02:53,511
Yeah.
Or a bowl of snot.

712
01:02:53,720 --> 01:02:55,233
You know what it really reminds me of?

713
01:02:57,000 --> 01:02:59,230
Tastee Wheat. Did you
ever eat Tastee Wheat?

714
01:02:59,840 --> 01:03:01,478
No, but technically,
neither did you.

715
01:03:01,720 --> 01:03:03,676
That's exactly my point.
Exactly.

716
01:03:03,920 --> 01:03:05,239
Because you have to wonder...

717
01:03:05,480 --> 01:03:08,597
...how do the machines really know
what Tastee Wheat tasted like. Huh!

718
01:03:08,840 --> 01:03:10,193
Maybe they got it wrong.

719
01:03:10,440 --> 01:03:13,512
Maybe what I think Tastee Wheat
tasted like actually tasted like...

720
01:03:13,800 --> 01:03:15,711
...oatmeal or tuna fish.

721
01:03:16,080 --> 01:03:18,799
That makes you wonder about a lot of things.
You take chicken, for example.

722
01:03:19,040 --> 01:03:20,951
Maybe they couldn't figure out
what to make chicken taste like...

723
01:03:21,200 --> 01:03:23,156
...which is why chicken tastes
like everything.

724
01:03:23,400 --> 01:03:25,118
- And maybe they...
- Shut up Mouse.

725
01:03:26,680 --> 01:03:28,079
It's a single-celled protein...

726
01:03:28,320 --> 01:03:31,232
...combined with synthetic aminos,
vitamins and minerals.

727
01:03:31,480 --> 01:03:32,674
Everything the body needs.

728
01:03:32,920 --> 01:03:35,673
It doesn't have everything
the body needs.

729
01:03:38,320 --> 01:03:41,278
So, I understand that you've run through
the agent training program.

730
01:03:42,280 --> 01:03:44,236
You know, I wrote that program.

731
01:03:44,520 --> 01:03:45,748
Here it comes.

732
01:03:46,000 --> 01:03:47,877
- What did you think of her?
- Of who?

733
01:03:48,240 --> 01:03:51,152
The woman in the red dress.
I designed her.

734
01:03:51,480 --> 01:03:54,119
She doesn't talk very much...

735
01:03:54,360 --> 01:03:58,148
...but if you'd like to meet her, I can
arrange a much more personal milieu.

736
01:03:58,400 --> 01:03:59,719
The digital pimp hard at work.

737
01:03:59,960 --> 01:04:02,110
Pay no attention to
these hypocrites, Neo.

738
01:04:03,360 --> 01:04:05,112
To deny our own impulses...

739
01:04:05,360 --> 01:04:08,352
...is to deny the very thing
that makes us human.

740
01:04:10,200 --> 01:04:11,519
Dozer, when you're done...

741
01:04:11,760 --> 01:04:13,113
...bring the ship up to broadcast depth.

742
01:04:13,800 --> 01:04:15,074
We're going in.

743
01:04:15,760 --> 01:04:17,113
I'm taking Neo to see her.

744
01:04:21,080 --> 01:04:22,069
See who?

745
01:04:23,040 --> 01:04:24,234
The Oracle.

746
01:04:29,520 --> 01:04:30,999
Everyone, please observe...

747
01:04:31,320 --> 01:04:33,914
...the "fasten seat belt" and "no smoking"
signs are being turned on.

748
01:04:34,400 --> 01:04:37,631
Sit back and enjoy your flight.

749
01:05:00,960 --> 01:05:01,949
We're in.

750
01:05:17,040 --> 01:05:18,109
We'll be back in an hour.

751
01:05:32,320 --> 01:05:33,673
Unbelievable...

752
01:05:34,480 --> 01:05:35,754
...isn't it?

753
01:05:39,200 --> 01:05:40,952
- God!
- What?

754
01:05:41,600 --> 01:05:42,919
I used to eat there.

755
01:05:45,080 --> 01:05:46,638
Really good noodles.

756
01:05:51,240 --> 01:05:53,629
I have these memories from my life.

757
01:05:56,000 --> 01:05:57,592
None of them happened.

758
01:05:58,200 --> 01:05:59,474
What does that mean?

759
01:05:59,720 --> 01:06:01,836
That the Matrix cannot tell you
who you are.

760
01:06:02,720 --> 01:06:03,869
But an oracle can?

761
01:06:04,320 --> 01:06:05,469
That's different.

762
01:06:10,040 --> 01:06:12,110
Did you go to her?

763
01:06:12,680 --> 01:06:13,795
Yes.

764
01:06:14,280 --> 01:06:15,599
What did she tell you?

765
01:06:18,720 --> 01:06:20,153
She told me...

766
01:06:21,160 --> 01:06:22,275
What?

767
01:06:25,920 --> 01:06:28,194
We're here. Neo.

768
01:06:28,400 --> 01:06:29,753
Come with me.

769
01:06:48,920 --> 01:06:51,309
So is this the same oracle
that made the.....

770
01:06:51,309 --> 01:06:52,595
......prophecy?

771
01:06:52,840 --> 01:06:56,992
Yes. She's very old. She's been
with us since the beginning.

772
01:06:57,440 --> 01:06:59,999
- The beginning?
- Of the Resistance.

773
01:07:01,520 --> 01:07:03,795
And she knows what? Everything?

774
01:07:05,760 --> 01:07:07,591
She would say she knows enough.

775
01:07:08,680 --> 01:07:10,398
And she's never wrong.

776
01:07:12,520 --> 01:07:15,557
Try not to think of it
in terms of right and wrong.

777
01:07:15,880 --> 01:07:17,393
She is a guide, Neo.

778
01:07:17,760 --> 01:07:19,557
She can help you to find the path.

779
01:07:20,120 --> 01:07:21,235
She helped you?

780
01:07:23,640 --> 01:07:24,914
What did she tell you?

781
01:07:27,280 --> 01:07:29,396
That I would find the One.

782
01:07:42,000 --> 01:07:44,036
I told you I can only
show you the door.

783
01:07:44,720 --> 01:07:46,711
You have to walk through it.

784
01:07:50,360 --> 01:07:51,395
Hello, Neo.

785
01:07:51,640 --> 01:07:53,232
You're right on time.

786
01:08:00,840 --> 01:08:04,469
Make yourself at home, Morpheus.
Neo, come with me.

787
01:08:09,920 --> 01:08:11,433
These are the other Potentials.

788
01:08:11,680 --> 01:08:13,159
You can wait here.

789
01:08:52,320 --> 01:08:54,754
Do not try and bend the spoon.

790
01:08:55,120 --> 01:08:57,156
That's impossible.

791
01:08:57,960 --> 01:09:01,794
Instead, only try
to realize the truth.

792
01:09:02,320 --> 01:09:03,639
What truth?

793
01:09:03,880 --> 01:09:05,472
There is no spoon.

794
01:09:07,960 --> 01:09:09,234
There is no spoon?

795
01:09:09,480 --> 01:09:13,792
Then you'll see that it is not the spoon
that bends. It is only yourself.

796
01:09:29,160 --> 01:09:30,593
The Oracle will see you now.

797
01:09:40,840 --> 01:09:42,319
I know you're Neo.

798
01:09:42,920 --> 01:09:44,035
Be right with you.

799
01:09:45,040 --> 01:09:47,315
- You're the Oracle?
- Bingo.

800
01:09:49,920 --> 01:09:52,673
Not quite what you
were expecting, right?

801
01:09:53,680 --> 01:09:55,750
Almost done.

802
01:09:58,160 --> 01:09:59,718
Smell good, don't they?

803
01:10:02,360 --> 01:10:04,112
I'd ask you to sit down...

804
01:10:04,360 --> 01:10:06,635
...but you're not going to anyway.

805
01:10:07,120 --> 01:10:09,873
- And don't worry about the vase.
- What vase?

806
01:10:12,880 --> 01:10:13,995
That vase.

807
01:10:14,920 --> 01:10:15,909
I'm sorry.

808
01:10:16,160 --> 01:10:17,957
I said, don't worry about it.

809
01:10:19,080 --> 01:10:20,957
I'll get one of my kids to fix it.

810
01:10:21,560 --> 01:10:22,709
How did you know?

811
01:10:24,680 --> 01:10:28,309
What's really going to bake
your noodle later on is...

812
01:10:28,640 --> 01:10:31,473
...would you still have broken it
if I hadn't said anything?

813
01:10:36,080 --> 01:10:37,911
You're cuter than I thought.

814
01:10:40,840 --> 01:10:42,990
I can see why she likes you.

815
01:10:43,840 --> 01:10:44,875
Who?

816
01:10:45,120 --> 01:10:46,872
Not too bright, though.

817
01:10:50,040 --> 01:10:52,998
You know why Morpheus
brought you to see me.

818
01:10:55,040 --> 01:10:56,155
So...

819
01:10:57,080 --> 01:10:58,399
...what do you think?

820
01:11:00,160 --> 01:11:01,832
Do you think you are the One?

821
01:11:03,720 --> 01:11:04,709
Honestly. I don't know.

822
01:11:08,000 --> 01:11:09,353
You know what that means?

823
01:11:10,160 --> 01:11:11,275
It's Latin.

824
01:11:11,640 --> 01:11:13,756
Means, "Know thyself."

825
01:11:15,160 --> 01:11:17,037
I'll let you in on a little secret.

826
01:11:19,200 --> 01:11:22,875
Being the One is just
like being in love.

827
01:11:23,560 --> 01:11:26,313
No one can tell you you're in love.
You just know it...

828
01:11:26,560 --> 01:11:27,629
...through and through.

829
01:11:27,960 --> 01:11:29,916
Balls to bones.

830
01:11:32,360 --> 01:11:34,157
Well...

831
01:11:35,040 --> 01:11:37,031
...I'd better have a look at you.

832
01:11:38,320 --> 01:11:39,753
Open your mouth. Say, "Ah."

833
01:11:53,560 --> 01:11:55,152
Okay...

834
01:11:55,760 --> 01:12:00,515
Now I'm supposed to say,
"Hmm, that's interesting, but..."

835
01:12:01,000 --> 01:12:02,069
Then you say:

836
01:12:02,640 --> 01:12:03,868
But what?

837
01:12:04,120 --> 01:12:07,908
But you already know
what I'm going to tell you.

838
01:12:09,280 --> 01:12:12,113
- I'm not the One.
- Sorry, kid.

839
01:12:13,680 --> 01:12:15,591
You got the gift...

840
01:12:16,560 --> 01:12:18,676
...but it looks like
you're waiting for something.

841
01:12:23,360 --> 01:12:27,148
- What?
- Your next life, maybe. Who knows?

842
01:12:27,720 --> 01:12:29,870
That's the way these things go.

843
01:12:30,720 --> 01:12:33,188
- What's funny?
- Morpheus.

844
01:12:36,520 --> 01:12:38,158
He almost had me convinced.

845
01:12:38,400 --> 01:12:39,469
I know.

846
01:12:40,960 --> 01:12:42,996
Poor Morpheus.

847
01:12:45,280 --> 01:12:48,272
Without him, we're lost.

848
01:12:49,760 --> 01:12:51,830
What do you mean, "without him"?

849
01:12:55,680 --> 01:12:57,511
Are you sure you want
to hear this?

850
01:12:59,640 --> 01:13:02,279
Morpheus believes in you, Neo.

851
01:13:03,920 --> 01:13:05,990
And no one, not you, not even me...

852
01:13:06,240 --> 01:13:08,390
...can convince him otherwise.

853
01:13:08,760 --> 01:13:11,035
He believes it so blindly...

854
01:13:11,320 --> 01:13:15,472
...that he's going to sacrifice
his life to save yours.

855
01:13:15,720 --> 01:13:19,508
- What?
- You're going to have to make a choice.

856
01:13:20,120 --> 01:13:23,556
In the one hand,
you'll have Morpheus' life.

857
01:13:24,040 --> 01:13:26,793
And in the other hand,
you'll have your own.

858
01:13:28,160 --> 01:13:30,355
One of you is going to die.

859
01:13:32,360 --> 01:13:35,511
Which one will be up to you.

860
01:13:36,840 --> 01:13:38,671
I'm sorry, kiddo. I really am.

861
01:13:38,920 --> 01:13:40,512
You have a good soul.

862
01:13:41,560 --> 01:13:44,154
And I hate giving
good people bad news.

863
01:13:47,160 --> 01:13:48,559
Don't worry about it.

864
01:13:48,800 --> 01:13:51,109
As soon as you
step outside that door...

865
01:13:51,360 --> 01:13:53,396
...you'll start feeling better.

866
01:13:54,080 --> 01:13:57,709
You'll remember you don't believe
in any of this fate crap.

867
01:13:58,520 --> 01:14:01,159
You're in control of your own life.

868
01:14:01,960 --> 01:14:03,188
Remember?

869
01:14:05,000 --> 01:14:06,592
Here...

870
01:14:07,760 --> 01:14:09,239
...take a cookie.

871
01:14:09,760 --> 01:14:12,957
I promise, by the time
you're done eating it...

872
01:14:13,880 --> 01:14:16,155
...you'll feel right as rain.

873
01:14:25,000 --> 01:14:26,274
What was said...

874
01:14:26,880 --> 01:14:28,279
...was for you...

875
01:14:28,800 --> 01:14:30,552
...and for you alone.

876
01:14:52,560 --> 01:14:53,629
They're on the way.

877
01:15:22,200 --> 01:15:23,189
What is that?

878
01:15:37,360 --> 01:15:38,713
Oh, déjà vu.

879
01:15:42,080 --> 01:15:43,115
What did you just say?

880
01:15:43,360 --> 01:15:44,793
Nothing.
Just said a little déjà vu.

881
01:15:45,040 --> 01:15:46,598
- What did you see?
- What happened?

882
01:15:47,960 --> 01:15:50,030
A black cat went past us...

883
01:15:50,280 --> 01:15:51,838
...and then another that look just like it.

884
01:15:52,080 --> 01:15:53,559
How much like it.
Was it the same cat?

885
01:15:54,480 --> 01:15:55,629
Might it be.
I'm not sure.

886
01:15:56,400 --> 01:15:58,118
Switch, Apoc.

887
01:16:01,280 --> 01:16:02,269
What is it?

888
01:16:02,520 --> 01:16:06,752
A déjà vu is usually a glitch in the Matrix.
It happened when they change something.

889
01:16:09,800 --> 01:16:10,789
Oh, my God.

890
01:16:12,560 --> 01:16:14,551
Let's go.

891
01:16:18,520 --> 01:16:20,192
They cut the hard line.
It's a trap! Get out!

892
01:16:25,520 --> 01:16:26,669
Oh, no.

893
01:16:28,080 --> 01:16:29,069
Oh, no.

894
01:17:04,320 --> 01:17:07,675
Ah! That's what they changed.
We're trapped. There is no way out.

895
01:17:07,920 --> 01:17:09,717
Be calm. Give me your phone.

896
01:17:09,960 --> 01:17:11,439
They'll be able to track it.

897
01:17:11,680 --> 01:17:13,033
We have no choice.

898
01:17:14,400 --> 01:17:15,549
Operator. Tank.

899
01:17:15,880 --> 01:17:18,599
{\i1}Find a structural drawing of
this building. Find it fast.{\i}

900
01:17:26,120 --> 01:17:28,588
{\i1}- Got it!
- I need the main wet-wall.{\i}

901
01:17:31,480 --> 01:17:32,515
Eighth floor.

902
01:17:32,720 --> 01:17:34,233
{\i1}They're on the eighth floor.{\i}

903
01:17:34,520 --> 01:17:35,919
Switch, straight ahead.

904
01:17:43,640 --> 01:17:45,710
I hope the Oracle
gave you some good news.

905
01:17:53,640 --> 01:17:55,073
{\i1}Now left. That's it.{\i}

906
01:17:55,360 --> 01:17:56,349
Good.

907
01:18:05,680 --> 01:18:06,908
Where are they?

908
01:19:04,880 --> 01:19:05,995
They're in the walls.

909
01:19:07,400 --> 01:19:08,515
In the walls!

910
01:19:29,040 --> 01:19:30,678
It's an agent!

911
01:19:36,740 --> 01:19:41,777
Morpheus. Trinity. You must get Neo out!
He's all that matters!

912
01:19:41,777 --> 01:19:43,209
No.
No, Morpheus! Don't!

913
01:19:43,460 --> 01:19:44,939
Trinity, go!

914
01:19:44,939 --> 01:19:45,689
Go!

915
01:19:52,380 --> 01:19:54,211
- We can't leave him!
- We have to!

916
01:20:17,460 --> 01:20:20,371
Cypher.
Come on!

917
01:20:23,980 --> 01:20:27,655
The great Morpheus.
We meet at last.

918
01:20:28,180 --> 01:20:29,249
And you are?

919
01:20:29,500 --> 01:20:31,172
A Smith.

920
01:20:31,420 --> 01:20:32,648
Agent Smith.

921
01:20:33,220 --> 01:20:35,176
You all look the same to me.

922
01:21:21,780 --> 01:21:22,999
Take him.

923
01:21:29,540 --> 01:21:30,768
No.

924
01:21:35,760 --> 01:21:37,999
{\i1}- Operator.
- Yeah. I need an exit, fast.{\i}

925
01:21:37,999 --> 01:21:42,318
Cypher. Yeah. There was an accident.
Goddamn....car accident.

926
01:21:42,640 --> 01:21:44,358
{\i1}All of a sudden, boom.{\i}

927
01:21:44,600 --> 01:21:46,160
Somebody up there still likes me.

928
01:21:46,160 --> 01:21:47,354
I got you.

929
01:21:47,840 --> 01:21:49,671
{\i1} CYPHER.
Just get me out of here fast.{\i}

930
01:21:49,920 --> 01:21:52,720
Nearest exit, Franklin and Erie.
An old TV repair shop.

931
01:21:52,720 --> 01:21:53,709
Right.

932
01:21:56,720 --> 01:21:58,233
{\i1}- Operator.
- Tank, it's me.{\i}

933
01:21:58,480 --> 01:21:59,595
Is Morpheus alive?

934
01:21:59,960 --> 01:22:01,188
Is Morpheus alive, Tank?

935
01:22:01,600 --> 01:22:03,640
{\i1}Yes. They're moving him.
I don 't know where to, Yet.{\i}

936
01:22:03,640 --> 01:22:07,200
- He's alive. We need an exit.
- You're not far from Cypher.

937
01:22:07,200 --> 01:22:08,720
{\i1}- Cypher?
- I know.{\i}

938
01:22:08,720 --> 01:22:10,999
{\i1}- I sent him to Franklin and Erie.
- Got it.{\i}

939
01:22:19,440 --> 01:22:20,589
Got him.

940
01:22:31,080 --> 01:22:32,069
Where are they?

941
01:22:32,320 --> 01:22:33,514
Making the call.

942
01:22:34,160 --> 01:22:35,275
Good.

943
01:22:48,280 --> 01:22:49,998
You first Neo.

944
01:22:52,120 --> 01:22:53,314
Shit!

945
01:22:57,120 --> 01:22:59,314
Tank...
[SCREAMING] No............

946
01:23:01,640 --> 01:23:03,710
I don't know. It just went dead.

947
01:23:29,440 --> 01:23:30,589
{\i1}Hello, Trinity.{\i}

948
01:23:31,000 --> 01:23:32,999
Cypher? Where's Tank?

949
01:23:37,640 --> 01:23:38,629
You know...

950
01:23:40,280 --> 01:23:42,316
...for a long time...

951
01:23:43,480 --> 01:23:46,278
...I thought I was in love with you.

952
01:23:47,000 --> 01:23:48,956
{\i1}I used to dream about you.{\i}

953
01:23:50,000 --> 01:23:52,594
You're a beautiful woman, Trinity.

954
01:23:52,840 --> 01:23:55,600
{\i1}Too bad things had to
turn out this way.{\i}

955
01:23:55,600 --> 01:23:56,999
You killed them.

956
01:23:56,999 --> 01:23:58,800
- What?
- Oh, God.

957
01:23:58,800 --> 01:24:00,153
I'm tired, Trinity.

958
01:24:01,520 --> 01:24:03,317
I'm tired of this war...

959
01:24:03,600 --> 01:24:06,319
...tired of fighting.
I'm tired of this ship...

960
01:24:06,640 --> 01:24:11,077
...of being cold, of eating
the same goddamn goop every day.

961
01:24:13,280 --> 01:24:14,840
But most of all...

962
01:24:14,840 --> 01:24:18,500
{\i1}... I'm tired of that jackoff
and all of his bullshit.{\i}

963
01:24:19,160 --> 01:24:20,600
Surprise, asshole!

964
01:24:20,920 --> 01:24:23,280
I bet you never saw this coming...

965
01:24:23,280 --> 01:24:24,269
...did you?

966
01:24:26,480 --> 01:24:28,755
God, I wish I could be there...

967
01:24:29,320 --> 01:24:30,753
...when they break you.

968
01:24:31,760 --> 01:24:34,797
I wish I could walk in
just when it happens...

969
01:24:35,480 --> 01:24:37,118
...so right then...

970
01:24:37,360 --> 01:24:39,040
...you'd know it was me.

971
01:24:39,040 --> 01:24:42,440
{\i1}- You gave them Morpheus.
- He lied to us, Trinity.{\i}

972
01:24:42,440 --> 01:24:43,873
He tricked us!

973
01:24:44,400 --> 01:24:46,311
If you would told us the truth...

974
01:24:46,560 --> 01:24:49,313
...we would've told you to shove
that red pill right up your ass!

975
01:24:49,560 --> 01:24:52,711
{\i1}- That is not true, Cypher. He set us free.
- "Free."{\i}

976
01:24:52,960 --> 01:24:54,598
You call this free?

977
01:24:56,920 --> 01:24:59,309
All I do is what he tells me to do.

978
01:25:00,840 --> 01:25:03,638
If I had to choose between
that and the Matrix...

979
01:25:04,760 --> 01:25:05,999
...I choose the Matrix.

980
01:25:05,999 --> 01:25:08,000
The Matrix isn't real.

981
01:25:08,000 --> 01:25:09,600
{\i1}I disagree, Trinity.{\i}

982
01:25:09,600 --> 01:25:11,750
I think the Matrix...

983
01:25:12,080 --> 01:25:14,548
...can be more real than this world.

984
01:25:16,640 --> 01:25:19,029
All I do is pull the plug here.

985
01:25:19,280 --> 01:25:20,554
But there...

986
01:25:21,080 --> 01:25:23,275
{\i1}... you have to watch Apoc die.{\i}

987
01:25:24,400 --> 01:25:25,600
Trinity.

988
01:25:27,500 --> 01:25:28,600
No.

989
01:25:30,720 --> 01:25:32,500
{\i1}Welcome to the real world.
Huh! baby.{\i}

990
01:25:32,500 --> 01:25:33,800
But you're out.
Cypher.

991
01:25:33,800 --> 01:25:36,109
{\i1}- You can 't go back.
- Oh! No, That's what you think.{\i}

992
01:25:36,360 --> 01:25:37,793
{\i1}They are going to reinsert my body.{\i}

993
01:25:38,040 --> 01:25:41,760
{\i1}I go back to sleep and When I wake up,
I won't remember a goddamn thing.{\i}

994
01:25:41,760 --> 01:25:42,829
By the way...

995
01:25:42,829 --> 01:25:45,798
...if you have anything terribly important
to say to Switch...

996
01:25:46,280 --> 01:25:48,600
{\i1}...I suggest you say it now.
- No, please don't.{\i}

997
01:25:48,920 --> 01:25:50,478
Not like this.

998
01:25:52,120 --> 01:25:53,678
Not like this.

999
01:25:57,960 --> 01:25:58,949
Too late.

1000
01:25:59,400 --> 01:26:00,913
Goddamn you, Cypher!

1001
01:26:01,160 --> 01:26:02,957
Don't hate me, Trinity.

1002
01:26:03,320 --> 01:26:05,117
I'm just a messenger.

1003
01:26:05,520 --> 01:26:08,557
And right now,
I'm going to prove it to you.

1004
01:26:09,600 --> 01:26:11,192
If Morpheus was right...

1005
01:26:11,720 --> 01:26:13,800
...and there's no way
I can pull this plug.

1006
01:26:14,080 --> 01:26:15,513
{\i1}I mean If Neo's the One...{\i}

1007
01:26:16,000 --> 01:26:20,500
....then there'd have to be
some kind of a miracle to stop me.

1008
01:26:20,960 --> 01:26:22,234
Right?

1009
01:26:22,234 --> 01:26:25,999
I mean, how can he be the One
if he's dead?

1010
01:26:26,920 --> 01:26:29,070
{\i1}You never did answer me before...{\i}

1011
01:26:29,360 --> 01:26:31,590
{\i1}... if you bought into
Morpheus ' bullshit.{\i}

1012
01:26:31,960 --> 01:26:35,032
Come on. All I want
is a little yes or no.

1013
01:26:36,360 --> 01:26:38,590
Look into his eyes...

1014
01:26:39,320 --> 01:26:41,500
{\i1}... those big, pretty eyes...{\i}

1015
01:26:43,400 --> 01:26:44,674
...and tell me...

1016
01:26:45,360 --> 01:26:46,588
{\i1}... yes...{\i}

1017
01:26:46,880 --> 01:26:48,199
{\i1}... or no.{\i}

1018
01:26:49,440 --> 01:26:50,509
Yes.

1019
01:26:50,509 --> 01:26:52,700
No.
I don't believe it.

1020
01:26:53,560 --> 01:26:58,111
Believe it or not, you piece of shit,
you're still going to burn!

1021
01:27:15,760 --> 01:27:16,954
You first.

1022
01:27:24,680 --> 01:27:25,669
You're hurt.

1023
01:27:26,000 --> 01:27:27,035
I'll be all right.

1024
01:27:29,720 --> 01:27:30,835
Dozer?

1025
01:27:48,360 --> 01:27:50,935
Have you ever stood and stared at it?

1026
01:27:51,480 --> 01:27:54,472
Marveled at its beauty...

1027
01:27:54,840 --> 01:27:56,990
...its genius?

1028
01:27:58,120 --> 01:27:59,917
Billions of people...

1029
01:28:00,160 --> 01:28:02,799
...just living out their lives.

1030
01:28:03,800 --> 01:28:05,392
Oblivious.

1031
01:28:09,800 --> 01:28:12,553
Did you know that the first Matrix...

1032
01:28:12,800 --> 01:28:17,316
...was designed to be a perfect
human world where none suffered...

1033
01:28:17,760 --> 01:28:20,558
...where everyone would be happy.

1034
01:28:21,080 --> 01:28:22,513
It was a disaster.

1035
01:28:22,760 --> 01:28:26,912
No one would accept the program.
Entire crops were lost.

1036
01:28:27,760 --> 01:28:29,432
Some believe that...

1037
01:28:29,680 --> 01:28:33,878
...we lacked the programming language
to describe your perfect world.

1038
01:28:34,120 --> 01:28:36,873
But I believe that, as a species...

1039
01:28:37,120 --> 01:28:40,795
...human beings define
their reality through misery...

1040
01:28:41,040 --> 01:28:42,359
...and suffering.

1041
01:28:42,600 --> 01:28:45,194
So the perfect world was a dream...

1042
01:28:45,440 --> 01:28:50,070
...that your primitive cerebrum
kept trying to wake up from.

1043
01:28:51,360 --> 01:28:54,875
Which is why the Matrix was
redesigned to this.

1044
01:28:55,320 --> 01:28:56,753
The peak...

1045
01:28:57,000 --> 01:28:58,353
...of your civilization.

1046
01:28:58,600 --> 01:29:00,750
I say, "your civilization"...

1047
01:29:01,000 --> 01:29:04,959
...because as soon as we started thinking
for you, it really became our civilization...

1048
01:29:05,200 --> 01:29:08,158
...which is, of course,
what this is all about.

1049
01:29:09,440 --> 01:29:11,908
Evolution, Morpheus.

1050
01:29:12,200 --> 01:29:13,474
Evolution.

1051
01:29:15,680 --> 01:29:17,477
Like the dinosaur.

1052
01:29:19,560 --> 01:29:21,118
Look out that window.

1053
01:29:21,800 --> 01:29:23,836
You had your time.

1054
01:29:24,520 --> 01:29:28,274
The future is our world, Morpheus.

1055
01:29:28,600 --> 01:29:30,875
The future is our time.

1056
01:29:34,680 --> 01:29:36,500
There could be a problem.

1057
01:29:36,960 --> 01:29:40,191
- What are they doing to him?
- They're breaking into his mind.

1058
01:29:40,440 --> 01:29:42,760
It's like hacking a computer.
All it takes is time.

1059
01:29:42,760 --> 01:29:43,909
How much time?

1060
01:29:44,160 --> 01:29:47,300
Depends on the mind.
But eventually, it'll crack...

1061
01:29:47,300 --> 01:29:51,632
...and his alpha patterns
will change from this to this.

1062
01:29:51,880 --> 01:29:54,713
When it does, Morpheous will tell them
anything they want to know.

1063
01:29:54,960 --> 01:29:55,949
And what do they want?

1064
01:29:56,200 --> 01:30:00,079
The leader of every ship is given codes
to Zion's mainframe computer.

1065
01:30:00,320 --> 01:30:03,118
If an agent got the codes
and got into Zion's mainframe...

1066
01:30:03,360 --> 01:30:06,318
...they could destroy us.
We can't let that happen.

1067
01:30:06,318 --> 01:30:08,678
Trinity.
Zion's more important than me...

1068
01:30:08,678 --> 01:30:09,989
...or you...

1069
01:30:09,989 --> 01:30:11,999
...or even Morpheus.

1070
01:30:14,960 --> 01:30:16,960
Well, there has to be
something that we can do.

1071
01:30:16,960 --> 01:30:18,999
There is. We pull the plug.

1072
01:30:21,840 --> 01:30:23,760
You're going to kill him?

1073
01:30:23,760 --> 01:30:24,999
Kill Morpheus?

1074
01:30:25,480 --> 01:30:27,700
We don't have any other choice.

1075
01:30:33,560 --> 01:30:36,600
Never send a human
to do a machine's job.

1076
01:30:36,600 --> 01:30:38,530
If the Indedian insider has failed...

1077
01:30:38,530 --> 01:30:41,840
...they'll sever the connection
as soon as possible, unless...

1078
01:30:41,840 --> 01:30:43,720
They're dead. In either case...

1079
01:30:43,720 --> 01:30:47,110
We have no choice. But continue as planned.
Deploy the sentinels.

1080
01:30:47,360 --> 01:30:48,395
Immediately.

1081
01:30:53,440 --> 01:30:56,000
Morpheus, you were more
than a leader to us.

1082
01:30:56,920 --> 01:30:59,600
You were.... a father.

1083
01:31:00,520 --> 01:31:02,397
We'll miss you always.

1084
01:31:08,880 --> 01:31:10,154
Stop!

1085
01:31:11,320 --> 01:31:12,720
I don't believe this is happening.

1086
01:31:12,720 --> 01:31:14,999
- Neo, this has to be done.
- Does it?

1087
01:31:15,440 --> 01:31:16,900
I don't know.
I.....

1088
01:31:16,900 --> 01:31:18,999
This can't be just coincidence.
It can't be.....

1089
01:31:18,999 --> 01:31:20,830
- What are you talking about?
- The Oracle.

1090
01:31:21,080 --> 01:31:22,798
She told me this would happen.

1091
01:31:23,200 --> 01:31:27,193
She told me that I would
have to make a choice.

1092
01:31:27,640 --> 01:31:28,834
What choice?

1093
01:31:31,680 --> 01:31:34,069
- What....what are you doing?
- I'm going in.

1094
01:31:34,400 --> 01:31:36,630
- No, you're not.
- I have to.

1095
01:31:36,840 --> 01:31:40,400
Neo, Morpheus sacrificed himself
so that we could get you out.

1096
01:31:40,400 --> 01:31:42,600
There is no way
that you're going back in.

1097
01:31:42,960 --> 01:31:46,999
Morpheus did what he did because
he believed that I'm something and I'm not.

1098
01:31:47,640 --> 01:31:50,757
- What?
- I'm not the One, Trinity.

1099
01:31:51,120 --> 01:31:53,999
- The Oracle hit me with that too.
- No, you have to be.

1100
01:31:54,200 --> 01:31:56,760
I'm sorry, I'm not.
I'm just another guy.

1101
01:31:57,400 --> 01:31:59,160
No, Neo, that's not true.

1102
01:31:59,160 --> 01:32:00,434
It can't be true.

1103
01:32:00,760 --> 01:32:01,760
Why?

1104
01:32:05,100 --> 01:32:09,360
Neo. This is loco. They've got Morpheus
in a military-controlled building.

1105
01:32:09,360 --> 01:32:13,800
Even if you somehow got inside, those
are agents holding him. Three of them.

1106
01:32:14,800 --> 01:32:18,554
I want Morpheus back too, but
what you're talking about is suicide.

1107
01:32:18,800 --> 01:32:21,473
I know that's what it looks like,
but it's not.

1108
01:32:21,720 --> 01:32:23,995
I can't explain to you why it's not.

1109
01:32:25,040 --> 01:32:28,840
Morpheus believed something, and
he was ready to give his life for it.

1110
01:32:28,840 --> 01:32:31,960
What he believed...I understand that now.
That's why I have to go.

1111
01:32:31,960 --> 01:32:34,394
- Why?
- Because I believe in something.

1112
01:32:34,600 --> 01:32:36,272
What?

1113
01:32:36,800 --> 01:32:38,600
I believe I can bring him back.

1114
01:32:54,720 --> 01:32:56,840
- What are you doing?
- Going with you.

1115
01:32:56,840 --> 01:32:59,718
- No, you're not.
- "No"?

1116
01:32:59,718 --> 01:33:01,916
Let me tell you what I believe.

1117
01:33:02,400 --> 01:33:04,675
I believe Morpheus means more to me
than he does to you.

1118
01:33:05,000 --> 01:33:09,118
I believe if you are really serious about
saving him, you are going to need my help.

1119
01:33:09,360 --> 01:33:11,500
And since I am the ranking officer
on this ship......

1120
01:33:11,500 --> 01:33:14,700
...if you don't like it,
I believe you can go to hell.

1121
01:33:15,040 --> 01:33:17,349
Because you aren't going
anywhere else.

1122
01:33:17,760 --> 01:33:19,239
Tank...

1123
01:33:19,239 --> 01:33:20,515
...load us up.

1124
01:33:29,720 --> 01:33:32,871
I'd like to share
a revelation that I've had...

1125
01:33:33,280 --> 01:33:34,759
...during my time here.

1126
01:33:35,000 --> 01:33:38,834
It came to me when I tried
to classify your species...

1127
01:33:39,080 --> 01:33:41,230
...and I realized...

1128
01:33:41,480 --> 01:33:43,675
...that you're not actually mammals.

1129
01:33:45,800 --> 01:33:48,155
Every mammal on this planet...

1130
01:33:48,480 --> 01:33:53,190
...instinctively develops a natural
equilibrium with the surrounding environment.

1131
01:33:53,440 --> 01:33:55,192
But you humans do not.

1132
01:33:55,720 --> 01:33:59,110
You move to an area
and you multiply...

1133
01:33:59,360 --> 01:34:03,672
...and multiply until every
natural resource is consumed.

1134
01:34:04,000 --> 01:34:05,991
The only way you can survive...

1135
01:34:06,280 --> 01:34:09,113
...is to spread to another area.

1136
01:34:14,320 --> 01:34:17,073
There is another organism
on this planet...

1137
01:34:17,320 --> 01:34:19,197
...that follows the same pattern.

1138
01:34:19,800 --> 01:34:21,392
Do you know what it is?

1139
01:34:21,760 --> 01:34:23,512
A virus.

1140
01:34:24,800 --> 01:34:27,712
Human beings are a disease.

1141
01:34:28,080 --> 01:34:29,800
A cancer of this planet.

1142
01:34:29,800 --> 01:34:31,836
You are a plague.

1143
01:34:32,360 --> 01:34:35,193
And we are the cure.

1144
01:34:36,160 --> 01:34:37,900
Okay, so what do you need?

1145
01:34:38,120 --> 01:34:39,500
Besides a miracle.

1146
01:34:39,760 --> 01:34:40,909
Guns.

1147
01:34:41,600 --> 01:34:42,874
Lots of guns.

1148
01:34:52,400 --> 01:34:53,999
TRINITY.
Neo.

1149
01:34:55,200 --> 01:34:57,634
No one has ever done
anything like this.

1150
01:34:58,800 --> 01:35:00,631
That's why it's going to work.

1151
01:35:04,560 --> 01:35:06,800
Why isn't the serum working?

1152
01:35:06,800 --> 01:35:09,800
Perhaps we're asking
the wrong questions.

1153
01:35:11,200 --> 01:35:12,394
Leave me with him.

1154
01:35:14,880 --> 01:35:15,949
Now.

1155
01:35:26,720 --> 01:35:28,233
Hold on, Morpheus.

1156
01:35:28,480 --> 01:35:31,800
They're coming for you.
They're coming.

1157
01:35:33,360 --> 01:35:35,396
Can you hear me, Morpheus?

1158
01:35:35,640 --> 01:35:38,200
I'm going to be honest...

1159
01:35:38,560 --> 01:35:39,709
...with you.

1160
01:35:43,920 --> 01:35:45,273
I...

1161
01:35:46,000 --> 01:35:47,194
...hate...

1162
01:35:47,440 --> 01:35:49,317
...this place...

1163
01:35:49,640 --> 01:35:51,835
...this zoo...

1164
01:35:52,080 --> 01:35:53,149
...this prison...

1165
01:35:53,400 --> 01:35:56,680
...this reality,
whatever you want to call it.

1166
01:35:56,680 --> 01:35:58,875
I can't stand it any longer.

1167
01:35:59,600 --> 01:36:01,397
It's the smell.

1168
01:36:02,720 --> 01:36:04,517
If there is such a thing.

1169
01:36:04,840 --> 01:36:07,991
I feel saturated by it.

1170
01:36:09,440 --> 01:36:11,749
I can taste...

1171
01:36:12,560 --> 01:36:14,516
...your stink.

1172
01:36:14,760 --> 01:36:18,600
And every time I do, I fear that
I have somehow been infected by it.

1173
01:36:18,600 --> 01:36:20,158
It's repulsive.

1174
01:36:20,158 --> 01:36:21,639
Isn't it?

1175
01:36:23,720 --> 01:36:25,915
I must get out of here.

1176
01:36:26,320 --> 01:36:28,436
I must get free.

1177
01:36:28,680 --> 01:36:31,680
And in this mind is the key.

1178
01:36:31,680 --> 01:36:33,272
My key.

1179
01:36:33,520 --> 01:36:36,520
Once Zion is destroyed,
there is no need for me to be here.

1180
01:36:36,520 --> 01:36:38,078
Do you understand?

1181
01:36:38,360 --> 01:36:39,679
I need the codes.

1182
01:36:39,920 --> 01:36:42,150
I have to get inside Zion...

1183
01:36:42,480 --> 01:36:44,869
...and you have to tell me how.

1184
01:36:45,280 --> 01:36:47,077
You're going to tell me...

1185
01:36:47,320 --> 01:36:49,390
...or you're going to die.

1186
01:37:08,760 --> 01:37:13,599
Will you please remove any metallic items
you're carrying. Keys, loose change.

1187
01:37:15,520 --> 01:37:16,999
Holy shit!

1188
01:37:28,120 --> 01:37:30,714
Backup. Send backup.

1189
01:37:53,520 --> 01:37:54,999
COPS:
-Freeze!

1190
01:40:04,160 --> 01:40:06,196
What were you doing?

1191
01:40:06,880 --> 01:40:08,108
He doesn't know.

1192
01:40:08,360 --> 01:40:09,793
Know what?

1193
01:40:36,720 --> 01:40:39,109
I think they're trying to save him.

1194
01:40:53,360 --> 01:40:55,032
There is no spoon.

1195
01:41:23,440 --> 01:41:25,510
Find them and destroy them!

1196
01:41:27,080 --> 01:41:29,877
I repeat. We're under attack!

1197
01:41:59,600 --> 01:42:00,600
Trinity.

1198
01:42:01,280 --> 01:42:02,700
Help!

1199
01:42:23,400 --> 01:42:24,549
Only human.

1200
01:42:25,600 --> 01:42:27,397
Dodge this.

1201
01:42:39,200 --> 01:42:40,999
- How did you do that?
- Do what?

1202
01:42:40,999 --> 01:42:45,500
You moved like they do.
I've never seen anyone move that fast.

1203
01:42:45,880 --> 01:42:47,999
It wasn't fast enough.

1204
01:42:49,840 --> 01:42:51,068
Can you fly that thing?

1205
01:42:52,360 --> 01:42:54,078
Not yet.

1206
01:42:56,200 --> 01:42:57,269
Operator.

1207
01:42:57,480 --> 01:43:00,517
{\i1}Tank. I need a pilot program
for a B-212 helicopter.{\i}

1208
01:43:00,960 --> 01:43:02,188
{\i1}Hurry.{\i}

1209
01:43:09,800 --> 01:43:11,358
Let's go.

1210
01:43:25,840 --> 01:43:26,875
No.

1211
01:44:16,360 --> 01:44:19,874
Morpheus, get up.
Get up, get up.

1212
01:44:55,360 --> 01:44:57,032
He's not going to make it.

1213
01:45:05,760 --> 01:45:06,999
Got you.

1214
01:46:51,200 --> 01:46:52,553
I knew it.

1215
01:46:53,040 --> 01:46:54,700
He's the One.

1216
01:47:09,640 --> 01:47:11,999
Do you believe it now, Trinity?

1217
01:47:17,440 --> 01:47:19,317
The Oracle.

1218
01:47:19,317 --> 01:47:21,755
- She told me...
- She told you...

1219
01:47:22,120 --> 01:47:23,920
...Exactly what you needed to hear.

1220
01:47:23,920 --> 01:47:25,400
That's all.

1221
01:47:26,200 --> 01:47:29,033
Neo. Sooner or later you are going to
realize, just as I did...

1222
01:47:29,360 --> 01:47:31,555
...there's a difference
between knowing the path...

1223
01:47:32,280 --> 01:47:33,999
...and walking the path.

1224
01:47:36,440 --> 01:47:38,480
Operator.
Tank.

1225
01:47:38,480 --> 01:47:41,160
{\i1}- Goddamn. It's good to hear your voice, sir.
- We need an exit.{\i}

1226
01:47:41,160 --> 01:47:44,833
Got one ready. Subway station,
State and Balboa.

1227
01:47:55,760 --> 01:47:57,273
Damn it!

1228
01:47:57,520 --> 01:47:58,920
The trace was completed.

1229
01:47:58,920 --> 01:48:02,356
- We have their position.
- Sentinels are standing by.

1230
01:48:04,000 --> 01:48:05,700
Order the strike.

1231
01:48:11,720 --> 01:48:13,999
They're not out yet.

1232
01:48:24,360 --> 01:48:25,634
You first, Morpheus.

1233
01:48:45,480 --> 01:48:47,675
Neo, I want to tell you something...

1234
01:48:50,800 --> 01:48:54,999
...but I'm afraid of
what it could mean if I do.

1235
01:48:58,040 --> 01:49:01,999
Everything the Oracle
told me has come true.

1236
01:49:03,840 --> 01:49:05,700
Everything but this.

1237
01:49:06,680 --> 01:49:07,999
But what?

1238
01:49:33,000 --> 01:49:34,800
- What the hell just happened?
- An agent.

1239
01:49:34,800 --> 01:49:36,999
- You have to send me back.
- I can't.

1240
01:49:38,600 --> 01:49:40,511
Mr. Anderson.

1241
01:49:42,600 --> 01:49:44,919
Run, Neo. Run.

1242
01:49:49,000 --> 01:49:50,800
What is he doing?

1243
01:49:50,800 --> 01:49:52,994
He's beginning to believe.

1244
01:50:17,880 --> 01:50:19,199
You're empty.

1245
01:50:19,760 --> 01:50:20,988
So are you.

1246
01:50:52,800 --> 01:50:55,678
I'm going to enjoy watching you die...

1247
01:50:56,760 --> 01:50:57,749
...Mr. Anderson.

1248
01:51:35,040 --> 01:51:38,031
Jesus, he's killing him.

1249
01:52:59,280 --> 01:53:00,999
You hear that, Mr. Anderson?

1250
01:53:01,440 --> 01:53:04,699
That is the sound of inevitability.

1251
01:53:06,800 --> 01:53:09,997
It is the sound of your death.

1252
01:53:11,680 --> 01:53:13,800
Goodbye, Mr. Anderson.

1253
01:53:13,800 --> 01:53:15,599
My name...

1254
01:53:17,800 --> 01:53:19,756
...is Neo.

1255
01:53:51,180 --> 01:53:53,716
- What happened?
- I don't know. I lost him.

1256
01:53:55,200 --> 01:53:56,900
Oh, shit.

1257
01:54:08,280 --> 01:54:09,679
Sentinels.

1258
01:54:10,400 --> 01:54:12,950
- How long?
- Five, maybe six minutes.

1259
01:54:14,620 --> 01:54:16,590
Tank, charge the EMP.

1260
01:54:16,700 --> 01:54:20,900
- We can't use that until he's out.
- I know. Trinity. Don't worry.

1261
01:54:20,900 --> 01:54:22,160
He's gonna make it.

1262
01:54:22,160 --> 01:54:24,200
Flat or pumps? No, just...

1263
01:54:24,200 --> 01:54:26,600
What the shit? That's my phone!

1264
01:54:27,360 --> 01:54:28,873
That guy took my phone!

1265
01:54:31,160 --> 01:54:34,700
{\i1}- Got him! He's on the run.
- Mr. Wizard...{\i}

1266
01:54:34,700 --> 01:54:36,400
...get me the hell out of here!

1267
01:54:36,400 --> 01:54:39,699
{\i1}I got the patch and old exit.
Wabash and Lake.{\i}

1268
01:54:42,080 --> 01:54:43,672
Oh, shit!

1269
01:55:03,140 --> 01:55:05,999
huhhhhhh!
Help! Need a little help!

1270
01:55:07,366 --> 01:55:08,999
{\i1}The door.{\i}

1271
01:55:23,600 --> 01:55:25,200
{\i1}The door on your left.{\i}

1272
01:55:25,200 --> 01:55:27,899
{\i1}No.
Your other left!{\i}

1273
01:55:33,560 --> 01:55:34,999
{\i1}The back door.{\i}

1274
01:55:54,680 --> 01:55:55,899
Oh, no.

1275
01:55:57,360 --> 01:55:58,999
Here they come.

1276
01:56:26,700 --> 01:56:28,594
He's going to make it.

1277
01:56:37,400 --> 01:56:40,792
{\i1}The fire escape at the end
of the alley, room 303.{\i}

1278
01:57:14,500 --> 01:57:16,108
They're inside.

1279
01:57:18,080 --> 01:57:19,349
Hurry, Neo.

1280
01:58:12,120 --> 01:58:14,248
It can't be.

1281
01:58:20,840 --> 01:58:22,500
Check him.

1282
01:58:26,000 --> 01:58:27,999
He's gone.

1283
01:58:34,120 --> 01:58:36,799
Goodbye, Mr. Anderson.

1284
01:58:45,920 --> 01:58:48,597
I'm not afraid anymore.

1285
01:58:49,360 --> 01:58:51,050
The Oracle told me...

1286
01:58:51,050 --> 01:58:57,400
...that I'd fall in love with that the man.
The man that I love would be the One.

1287
01:58:59,000 --> 01:59:00,877
So you see...

1288
01:59:01,060 --> 01:59:03,471
...you can't be dead.

1289
01:59:04,800 --> 01:59:06,752
You can't be...

1290
01:59:08,240 --> 01:59:10,710
...because I love you.

1291
01:59:12,080 --> 01:59:13,918
You hear me?

1292
01:59:14,800 --> 01:59:16,392
I love you.

1293
01:59:39,360 --> 01:59:40,999
Now, get up.

1294
01:59:48,900 --> 01:59:49,999
No.

1295
02:00:15,240 --> 02:00:16,468
How?

1296
02:00:17,320 --> 02:00:18,899
He is the One.

1297
02:02:36,880 --> 02:02:38,518
{\i1}I know you're out there.{\i}

1298
02:02:38,760 --> 02:02:40,512
{\i1}I can feel you now.{\i}

1299
02:02:40,920 --> 02:02:42,638
{\i1}I know that you're afraid.{\i}

1300
02:02:42,880 --> 02:02:44,393
{\i1}You're afraid of us.{\i}

1301
02:02:44,720 --> 02:02:46,472
{\i1}You're afraid of change.{\i}

1302
02:02:47,640 --> 02:02:49,073
{\i1}I don't know the future.{\i}

1303
02:02:49,320 --> 02:02:51,788
{\i1}I didn't come here to tell you
how this is going to end.{\i}

1304
02:02:52,040 --> 02:02:54,873
{\i1}I came here to tell you
how it's going to begin.{\i}

1305
02:02:55,800 --> 02:02:57,313
{\i1}I am going to hang up this phone.{\i}

1306
02:02:57,560 --> 02:03:00,518
{\i1}And then I am going to show these people
what you don't want them to see.{\i}

1307
02:03:00,760 --> 02:03:02,557
{\i1}I'm going to show them a world...{\i}

1308
02:03:02,800 --> 02:03:04,472
{\i1}... without you.{\i}

1309
02:03:04,760 --> 02:03:08,230
{\i1}A world without rules and controls,
without borders or boundaries.{\i}

1310
02:03:08,480 --> 02:03:12,029
{\i1}A world where anything is possible.{\i}

1311
02:03:14,560 --> 02:03:15,834
{\i1}Where we go from there...{\i}

1312
02:03:16,080 --> 02:03:17,957
{\i1}... is a choice I leave to you.{\i}

